    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-medicine-clinician-educator/1209/100750391760": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180564 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is The expanding Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine (PCCSM) in the Department of Medicine at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California (USC) is seeking outstanding physicians to join our growing clinical faculty. We welcome applications from highly motivated clinicians who are committed to providing exceptional patient care, working collaboratively within a multidisciplinary team, and contributing to the education and training of residents and fellows. We are seeking full-time clinical faculty , offering opportunities to build a practice aligned with individual interests, expertise, and career goals. Candidates must be board certified in Internal Medicine and board certified or board eligible in Pulmonary Disease and/or Critical Care Medicine , with eligibility for medical licensure in the State of California. Successful candidates will demonstrate strong clinical skills, excellent communication and teamwork abilities, and a commitment to caring for a diverse and medically complex patient population across both academic and clinical settings. Clinical Responsibilities Faculty will participate in a broad range of clinical activities based on their area of expertise and the needs of the Division, including: Inpatient Pulmonary and Critical Care Medicine services Medical and surgical ICU coverage Inpatient pulmonary consultation services Diagnostic and therapeutic pulmonary procedures Care of patients with complex pulmonary and critical illness Outpatient pulmonary medicine practice Night coverage of the PCCM service line, provided within a collaborative, team-based model, working alongside a critical care fellow and/or physician extender Teaching and supervision of residents, fellows, and advanced practice providers Participation in multidisciplinary clinical programs and conferences Collaboration with physicians and clinical teams across Keck Medicine and USC The position offers the opportunity to practice in a sophisticated academic medical center environment with exposure to a diverse and complex patient population, including patients with advanced pulmonary disease, malignancies, and other high-acuity medical conditions. Academic and Professional Opportunities As members of the Keck School of Medicine faculty, physicians will have opportunities to participate in the education of medical students, residents, fellows, and other health care professionals. Faculty may also engage in quality improvement, program development, clinical research, and other academic activities based on their interests and career goals. Our Division is committed to developing innovative clinical programs and expanding access to high-quality pulmonary, critical care, and sleep medicine throughout the USC health system and the broader Los Angeles community. Compensation and Benefits We offer a highly competitive compensation package and excellent benefits . Academic rank, salary, and clinical responsibilities will be commensurate with experience, qualifications, and overall scope of the position . The annual base salary range for this position is $260,000-$280,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. This is an excellent opportunity to join a dynamic and growing academic division within one of the nation's leading medical schools and health systems while practicing in the diverse and vibrant Los Angeles community. Join the Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care and Sleep Medicine at USC and become part of a collaborative faculty dedicated to clinical excellence, education, innovation, and advancing the care of patients with complex pulmonary and critical illness. Job ID REQ20180564 Posted Date 09/17/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Central Processing Distribution Technician (Non-Certified) - CPD - Per Diem 8 Hour Variable Shift (Union) Glendale, California Save Job Registered Nurse - Geropsych - Per Diem 12 Hour Night Shift (Union) Glendale, California Save Job Patient Advocate - Service Excellence - Full Time 8 Hours Days (Non-Union, Exempt) Arcadia, California Save Job RN Supervisor (Cardiovascular) - Surge