    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/part-time-lecturer-architectural-history-and-theory/1209/101416164736": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer, Architectural History & Theory",
      "description": "Part-Time Lecturer, Architectural History & Theory at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Part-Time Lecturer, Architectural History & Theory Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20181302 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The School of Architecture of the University of Southern California seeks to appoint part-time lecturers to lead discussion sections for history and theory of architecture and/or history and theory of urbanism courses. Successful candidates will teach multiple seminar-style discussion sections for large lecture courses, assist with grading, and manage other course-related administrative tasks. Candidates must have an M.A. or M. Phil. in architectural history/theory or a related field and must be able to teach courses in the history and theory of architecture and urbanism. A Ph.D. in architectural history or a related field, or current enrollment in a Ph.D. program and a minimum of 2 years teaching experience is strongly preferred. This is an in-person teaching position, and candidates must be able to be on campus at least two days per week. Complete applications must include a letter of interest, CV, syllabi of courses candidate has taught or co-taught, recent teaching evaluations, and the names of three individuals who may be contacted by USC for a letter of reference. Referees should be able to speak to the candidate's teaching experience and abilities. Review of applications will begin immediately. Position(s) will remain open until filled. The core salary range for this position is $50.75-$66.41 per hour. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position; the candidate's work experience, education, training, and key skills; internal peer equity; federal, state, and local laws; contractual stipulations; grant funding; and external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20181302 Posted Date 10/01/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with US