    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/division-chief-of-gynecologic-oncology-associate-or-professor-of-clinical-obstetrics-and-gynecology/1209/101416163760": {
      "title": "Division Chief of Gynecologic Oncology-Associate or Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology",
      "description": "Division Chief of Gynecologic Oncology-Associate or Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Division Chief of Gynecologic Oncology-Associate or Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180713 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC) was founded in 1880 and is the largest private employer in the city of Los Angeles. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California is seeking a Division Chief of Gynecologic Oncology who is a fellowship trained, board certiﬁed gynecologic oncologist at the level of associate or professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology. This position is ideally suited to a mid-career faculty member. The Division Chief of Gynecologic Oncology functions as the academic, clinical, and administrative leader of the division, advancing excellence in patient care, research, education, faculty development, and strategic growth across the Keck Medicine health system. This physician leader must have dedication for teaching and training future gynecologist oncologist as part of our fellowship program. Responsibilities will include providing subspecialty care in gynecologic oncology, including surgery, in- and outpatient consultation, chemotherapy management, and in- and outpatient management of patients with gynecologic cancers. Qualiﬁcations: MD degree with completion of a 4-year ACGME accredited Ob/Gyn residency. Completion of Gynecologic Oncology Fellowship Board Certiﬁed in Obstetrics and Gynecology and American Board of OB/GYN in Gynecologic Oncology The successful candidate is expected to apply for a California medical license and be licensed to practice medicine in California by the time of appointment. Experience: Minimum of 5 years of progressive leadership experience in an academic medical environment Prior experience as Division Chief or Director, Medical Director, or comparable leadership role preferred Expertise in comprehensive gynecologic cancer management, including minimally invasive surgery and chemotherapy. Leadership & Scholarship- Demonstrated experience in leadership, teaching, and research; strong publication record and funding history Demonstrated success in: Faculty mentorship and development Research productivity and program building Financial and operational management Multidisciplinary collaboration within a cancer center structure Recruitment and retention of faculty Responsibilities: Division Chief Duties: Clinical Leadership: Lead a division of ﬁve gynecologic oncologists and two advanced practice providers Education & Training: Mentor and supervise residents, fellows, and students; ensure excellence in medical education and clinical training programs Research & Scholarship: The research responsibilities of this position include a track record of scholarship that is required for an academic promotion, including conducting and assisting in research projects and mentoring trainees; expansion of the current research portfolio within the division including development of high-impact research initiatives that inform clinical practice; secure research funding and publish in peer-reviewed journals Program Development: Expand and strengthen the division’s clinical, educational, and research programs; align with departmental and institutional strategic goals Collaboration: Partner with departmental and institutional leaders to set priorities, allocate resources, and foster a positive, inclusive team Clinical responsibilities: Scope: Balances clinical practice (70%–80% of time) with protected academic time for teaching and research, and administrative time for Division Chief duties. Provide comprehensive gynecologic oncology care, including open, robotic, and laparoscopic surgery, chemotherapy management, and consultation Collaborate in multidisciplinary cancer care with radiation oncology, pathology, genomics, palliative care, social work, and patient-navigation services Practice sites include Keck Medical Center of USC, USC Arcadia Hospital, USC Verdugo Hospital, and satellite clinics located in Arcadia, Pasadena, Verdugo Hills and Tarzana. The position oﬀers a salary with excellent university beneﬁts and an academic appointment at the Keck School of Medicine of USC commensurate with the level of training and experience. The annual base salary for this position is $450,000-$500,000. Additionally, the chosen candidate will receive a signing bonus, housing allowance, and relocation costs. When extending an oﬀer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Qualiﬁed candidates should respond with a letter of interest, CV, and three recommendation letters to Rizalyn Reynaldo, EdD (rizalyna.reynaldo@med.usc.edu), Chief Administrative Oﬃcer in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Recommendations letters should be addressed to Dr. Joseph Ouzounian, Daniel R. Mishell Jr. MD Endowed Professor and Chair, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. USC is an equal opportunity, aﬃrmative action employer. All qualiﬁed applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC will consider for employment all qualiﬁed applicants with criminal histories in a manner consistent with the requirements of the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring ordinance. Job ID REQ20180713 Posted Date 10/01/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team