    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/instructor-assistant-associate-professor-of-occupational-therapy-new-montrose-location/1209/92059712736": {
      "title": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Occupational Therapy (New Montrose location)",
      "description": "Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Occupational Therapy (New Montrose location) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Instructor/Assistant/Associate Professor of Occupational Therapy (New Montrose location) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20172066 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Division of Occupational Science and Occupational Therapy at the University of Southern California (USC) invites applications for multiple full-time clinical faculty positions at a new outpatient location in Montrose, CA . These positions support adult rehabilitation and Lifestyle Redesign services within USC Care and offer the opportunity to practice in a dynamic academic healthcare setting. The Division seeks clinicians with expertise in hand therapy, orthopedics, lymphedema therapy, and Lifestyle Redesign. Applicants should have experience working with adult physical rehabilitation populations and chronic conditions, and must hold a current license to practice occupational therapy in the state of California. Clinical responsibilities may include neurological and cognitive rehabilitation for conditions such as stroke, brain injury, and spinal cord injury; lymphedema management, with preference given to candidates who are Certified Lymphedema Therapists; musculoskeletal and orthopedic rehabilitation; and chronic condition management, with Lifestyle Redesign training and certification preferred. Faculty assignments will be determined based on clinical expertise, prior experience, and organizational needs, allowing clinicians to develop focused specialty practices or contribute across multiple service lines. These roles provide the opportunity to integrate patient care with program development, clinical instruction, and scholarly activity within an interdisciplinary academic environment. The anticipated start date for these positions is July 1, 2026. The annual base salary range is $80,000 to $115,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC will consider for employment all qualified applicants with criminal records in a manner consistent with applicable laws and regulations, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for employers and the Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and with due consideration for patient and student safety. Please refer to the Background Screening Policy Appendix D for specific employment screen implications for the position for which you are applying. Job ID REQ20172066 Posted Date 10/01/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More Jul