    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/associate-or-professor-tenured-tenure-track-open-rank/1209/101067462448": {
      "title": "Associate or Professor Tenured/Tenure Track",
      "description": "Associate or Professor Tenured/Tenure Track - Open Rank at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Associate or Professor Tenured/Tenure Track - Open Rank Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20180969 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Biomedical Sciences. This is a full-time, tenured or tenure-track faculty appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and academic accomplishments. We seek an accomplished and dynamic scientist with a Ph.D. or a DDS, DMD, or equivalent dental degree together with a Ph.D., and an outstanding record of innovative research in craniofacial biology, translational research, or both, relevant to human health and disease. The successful candidate will have a sustained record of producing high-impact research, securing competitive external funding, and providing successful mentorship to students, trainees, and junior faculty. Previous administrative or academic leadership experience is desirable but not required; candidates should demonstrate the vision, interpersonal skills, and commitment necessary to lead a multidisciplinary academic department. The Chair will provide strategic leadership for the department's research and educational missions; recruit and retain outstanding faculty, support the professional development and success of faculty, staff, students, and trainees; foster a collaborative and inclusive academic environment; and advance the department's national and international reputation. The Chair will also be expected to maintain an active and NIH-funded research program. The Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry offers a highly collaborative research environment, with strengths in craniofacial, skeletal, and developmental biology; molecular and cellular biology; cancer biology; microbiology and immunology; stem cell and regenerative medicine; biomineralization and biomaterials; and clinical and translational research. In addition, the successful candidate will have opportunities to explore multidisciplinary research with leading scientists throughout the broader USC community. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter describing their qualifications, research program, leadership experience, and vision for the department; a curriculum vitae; a research statement; a statement of mentoring and leadership philosophy; and arrange for three letters of reference as part of the application process. For more information and/or to apply: https://usccareers.usc.edu Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The Trojan Family Rewards: We pride ourselves on creating the BEST USC EXPERIENCE, and that begins with our employees! We offer a wide variety of benefits and programs that support our faculty and staff and their families. For more information please visit http://benefits.usc.edu This support advocates work-life balance and employee well-being. As members of the Trojan family, employees are connected by the traditions and history that make us proud to be Trojans! As an equal opportunity employer, USC values and promotes diversity, equity and inclusion in the workplace. The work culture thrives on mutual respect, trust, and synergy amongst all of its members. USC has great minds that transform the world with their talents and research. Will you be one? Join us! FIGHT ON! The annual salary range for this position is $180,000 - $200,000/year. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC will consider for employment all qualified applicants with criminal records in a manner consistent with applicable laws and regulations, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for employers and the Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and with due consideration for patient and student safety. Please refer to the Background Screening Policy Appendix D for specific employment screen implications for the position for which you are applying. Job ID REQ20180969 Posted Date 09/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Missi