    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-research-immunology-and-immune-therapeutics/1209/100501008304": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Research Immunology and Immune Therapeutics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Research Immunology and Immune Therapeutics at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Research Immunology and Immune Therapeutics Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178705 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Immunology and Immune Therapeutics at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California in Los Angeles, California invites applicants for a full-time non-tenure-track Assistant Professor of Research position in the field of immunometabolism. We seek an outstanding scientist with deep expertise in mass spectrometry-based metabolomics and to support and advance a highly collaborative immunometabolism research community. The successful candidate will provide scientific leadership in the application and development of state-of-the-art metabolomic technologies to investigate cellular and tissue metabolism in the context of immune responses. This position will play a central role in supporting faculty studying immunometabolism across diverse biological systems, including sterile inflammation, cancer, infectious diseases, and other immune-mediated disorders. Responsibilities The successful candidate will: • Lead the development, implementation, and optimization of mass spectrometry-based metabolomic and lipidomic workflows for cellular and tissue analyses. • Collaborate with investigators across the department to design, execute, and interpret metabolomic studies that address fundamental questions in immunometabolism. • Develop and apply advanced analytical approaches for metabolic flux analysis, including stable isotope tracer experiments and quantitative interpretation of isotopic labeling data. • Integrate metabolomic and lipidomic datasets with complementary multiomic platforms to generate mechanistic insights into immune cell fate and function. • Provide expertise in experimental design, quality control, data analysis, and interpretation for collaborative research projects. • Participate in the development of new methodologies and technologies that enhance the department's metabolomics capabilities. • Contribute to grant applications, collaborative publications, and the training of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and research staff in metabolomics methodologies. Required Qualifications • Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in biochemistry, analytical chemistry, metabolism, immunology, systems biology, or a related discipline. • Demonstrated expertise in mass spectrometry-based metabolomics and/or lipidomics. • Experience developing and implementing quantitative workflows for metabolic profiling of cells and tissues. • Strong record of collaborative research and scholarly productivity. Preferred Qualifications • Expertise with stable isotope tracer methodologies and metabolic flux analysis. • Experience with mathematical modeling and computational analysis of isotopic labeling data. • Experience integrating metabolomic, lipidomic, transcriptomic, proteomic, and/or other multiomic datasets. • Familiarity with bioinformatics and statistical methods for large-scale omics analyses. • Experience supporting collaborative research programs and working in multidisciplinary scientific environments. • Demonstrated ability to develop innovative analytical methods and translate them to biologically relevant applications. Environment The successful candidate will join a vibrant and highly collaborative research environment with investigators studying the metabolic regulation of immunity across a broad spectrum of disease models. The department has substantial strengths in immunometabolism, inflammation, cancer biology, host-pathogen interactions, and systems biology, providing numerous opportunities for interdisciplinary collaborations and methodological innovation. The position offers access to cutting-edge instrumentation and the opportunity to shape the strategic direction of metabolomics and lipidomics research across multiple federally funded programs. The annual base salary range for this position is $115,000-$125,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. Applicants should submit a letter of application, Curriculum Vitae, a statement of current and future research plans, and three letters of recommendation. Job ID REQ20178705 Posted Date 09/11/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non