    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/full-time-teaching-track-faculty-position-in-quantitative-and-computational-biology/1209/94300113920": {
      "title": "Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Quantitative and Computational Biology",
      "description": "Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Quantitative and Computational Biology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Quantitative and Computational Biology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174366 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Quantitative and Computational Biology (QCB) in the Dana and David Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences of the University of Southern California invites applications for a teaching-track faculty position, instructor or lecturer, of Quantitative and Computational Biology. The ideal candidate will have expertise in quantitative, computational, and statistical approaches to solve fundamental questions in biology and biomedicine. The teaching activities of the successful candidate will primarily entail the teaching of statistics courses, including multiple sections of QBIO 305 Statistics for Biological Sciences, as well as the teaching and development of other computational biology courses. It is expected for the successful candidate to have a track record as researcher and educator in quantitative approaches to biology and to have rigorous training in statistics or biostatistics. The successful candidate will join the QCB Department, a group of 12 tenured/tenure-track, teaching, and research core faculty members. The QCB Department has a 45-year history of computational biology research and education, including a rigorous Ph.D. program in Computational Biology and Bioinformatics with 60 students, a Master’s program in Quantitative and Computational Biology with 25 students, and an undergraduate major in Quantitative Biology with 130 students that represents modern biology education at the interface of biology, mathematics, and computer science. Members of the QCB Department work closely with other faculty in the Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences, the Viterbi School of Engineering, the Keck School of Medicine, and other USC schools. The QCB Department is located on the University Park Campus in Los Angeles, California. More information on the QCB Department can be found at: http://dornsife.usc.edu/qcb/ The anticipated start date is August 16, 2027. Applicants must have received a Ph.D. (or equivalent) degree by time of appointment and ideally have at least one semester experience as instructor of record of a computational biology course at a higher education institution. Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026. In order to be considered for this position, all candidates must apply via the \"Apply\" link at the top or bottom of this page. Please submit a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a teaching statement, 3 current external letters of recommendation, and any other evidence of teaching effectiveness, including available teaching evaluations. Please direct inquiries to Rokas Oginskis ( oginskis@usc.edu ) The annual base salary range for this position is $80,000 - $90,250. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20174366 Posted Date 04/23/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits &