    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/tenure-track-assistant-professor-positions/1209/100143263472": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions",
      "description": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179801 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions University of Southern California Suzanne Dworak-Peck School of Social Work Start Date: August 2027 About the USC Suzanne Dworak-Peck School of Social Work The Suzanne Dworak-Peck School of Social Work at the University of Southern California (USC) invites applicants to apply for a tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor level to join a community of scholars dedicated to social work research, education, and community partnerships. Our School and University are located in the heart of Los Angeles, one of the largest, most diverse, and culturally rich cities in the United States. Our faculty pursues research and scholarship to catalyze positive social impact and enhance the well-being of individuals, families, and communities. Research opportunities and collaborations are enhanced through seven research centers and institutes, two clinical centers, and transdisciplinary collaborations with the schools of medicine, gerontology, pharmacy, policy, engineering, education, and liberal arts, among others. Partnerships with community-based stakeholders including health care providers, programs serving justice-involved youth, public child welfare and mental health providers are also central to our work as a School. In fall 2026, the school welcomed incoming Dean Laura Abrams and launched our BSW program. We seek to grow our tenure-track faculty to enhance our local, national, and global scholarly impact. About the Positions To complement our existing strengths and further advance social work scholarship, we seek candidates with substantive focus and research and teaching experience in at least one of three areas: 1) social welfare policy and analysis; particularly focusing on poverty, the welfare state, and children and families; 2) child welfare policy or practice; and/or 3) technology, AI, and the future of social work. Across all areas, we welcome scholarship focused on the experiences of Black communities in the US and/or other racial and ethnic minority groups. Methodologically, we encourage applications from scholars with training in causal inference, experimental designs, and big data analytic approaches. We also welcome candidates who are interested in forging interdisciplinary collaborations with allied disciplines across the USC campus, such as the health sciences, public policy, and others. All candidates must demonstrate exceptional promise or evidence of impactful scientific research and publications. Assistant professor positions require on-campus presence as candidates will teach in our range of educational programs, including MSW, BSW, PhD, Doctor of Social Work (DSW), and Doctor of Social Innovation (DSI). Applicants should describe their portfolio of experience and excellence in teaching in social work. Candidates are required to have an MSW degree from a CSWE-accredited university and a PhD in social work/welfare or a related field. Two-years of post-MSW practice experience is preferred. Application Procedure To be considered for this position, candidates must submit application materials online. A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter describing their interest in the position and an overview of their research and teaching experiences, 2) a curriculum vitae, and 3) contact information for three professional references who can provide letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin in fall 2026. Applications will be considered until position(s) are filled. The annual base salary range for this position is $110,000-$130,000 based on a nine-month contract. When extending an offer of employment, USC considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. USC will consider for employment all qualified applicants with criminal records in a manner consistent with applicable laws and regulations, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for employers and the Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and with due consideration for patient and student safety. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources by phone at (213) 821-8100, or by email at uschr@usc.edu. Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. All other questions and information requests should be directed to the Office of Faculty Affairs in the USC Suzanne Dworak-Peck School of Social Work at ssw.facultyaffairs@usc.edu. The search committee chair is Dr. Ben Henwood, the Frances L. and Albert G. Feldman Professor of Social Policy and Health. Job ID REQ20179801 Posted Date 09/03/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Management Facilities Management and Constru