    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/adjunct-assistant-professor-of-clinical-dentistry/1209/99745515184": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor of Clinical Dentistry",
      "description": "Adjunct Assistant Professor of Clinical Dentistry at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Adjunct Assistant Professor of Clinical Dentistry Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179321 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) About the Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC Since 1897, the Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC has shaped talented students into outstanding dental professionals. Through challenging clinical education, cutting-edge research, and a commitment to service, Ostrow provides future oral health professionals with the skills they need to excel. We are committed to maintaining an environment of excellence and eminence, and this commitment shines through in all that we do. About the Role The Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC is seeking a skilled, part-time 20%, Adjunct Assistant Professor of Clinical Dentistry faculty position to join the Department of Advanced Periodontology team. This position plays a critical role in clinical teaching in the post-doctoral Advanced Periodontology Program. In this program, you will focus on diagnosis, risk assessment, treatment planning, and surgical periodontal and dental implant therapy. Direct faculty supervision is a required component of resident education, ensuring high-quality patient care while providing the hands-on clinical training necessary for residents to develop competency and meet program accreditation standards. This is an excellent opportunity to be part of a leading dental school that values collaboration, professional growth, and a commitment to excellence. Key Responsibilities Tech pre-doctoral Advanced periodontics (resident classes) Diagnosis Risk assessment Treatment Planning Surgical periodontal therapy Dental Implant therapy Laboratory instruction Clinical instruction Mentor and evaluate students Minimum Qualifications DDS degree Certificate in Periodontology from US accredited Periodontology program Valid California dental license Candidates with Diplomate Status (or Board eligible) from American Board of Periodontology and Masters of Since degree are considered favorably. At least 2 years in clinical periodontology and implant surgery Experience in resective and regenerative periodontal surgery Experience in periodontal mucogingival and plastic surgery Experience in implant surgery and implant site development, including autogenous as well as biomaterials regenerative procedures. Why Join Us? This role directly supports USC’s mission of excellence in education and patient care by ensuring students have the tools they need to succeed clinically and academically. You’ll be joining a collaborative team in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment where your contributions have a meaningful impact every day. The hourly base salary for this position is $41.20 - $43.00/hr When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. How to Appy? For information and to apply, interested applicants must submit a cover letter, complete curriculum vitae, and arrange to have three letters of reference sent to: https://usccareers.usc.edu Casey Chen, Ph.D. Professor and Co-Chair Department of Endodontics and Periodontics Associate Dean of Applied Biomedical and Clinical Sciences Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry University of Southern California 925 West 34th Street Los Angeles, CA 90089-0064 c/o: Denise Cortez Email: dmcortez@ostrow.usc.edu Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Job ID REQ20179321 Posted Date 08/26/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievemen