    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-associate-full-professor-of-stem-cell-biology-and-regenerative-medicine-cardiovascular-re/1209/98503542704": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine (Cardiovascular Regenerative Biology) Tenure Track",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine (Cardiovascular Regenerative Biology) Tenure Track at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine (Cardiovascular Regenerative Biology) Tenure Track Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177789 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) All-Ranks Faculty Position: Cardiovascular Regenerative Biology The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Stem Cell Biology and Regenerative Medicine (stemcell.keck.usc.edu) at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California invites applications for two new faculty positions at all ranks (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) in cardiovascular regenerative biology. We seek outstanding candidates whose work will advance the next generation of therapies for heart failure and cardiac injury, broadly defined. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, heart regeneration, revascularization, fibrosis and remodeling, cardiac immunobiology, gene and RNA therapeutics, disease modeling and pathogenesis, and drug discovery. We are particularly interested in investigators whose approaches complement and extend ongoing efforts in cardiomyocyte-based therapies, including those focused on tissue microenvironment, immune interactions, vascularization, and mechanisms of durable functional integration. Successful candidates will pursue innovative, collaborative, and translational research programs that bridge mechanistic and data-driven approaches across molecular, cellular, tissue, and systems-level biology. Faculty will be core members of the newly established USC REPAIR Institute, a multidisciplinary, AI-enabled therapeutics development initiative spanning the Schools of Medicine, Engineering, and Pharmacy. REPAIR integrates strengths in pluripotent stem cell biology, nanoparticle-based delivery, RNA therapeutics, microphysiological systems, computational modeling and AI, pharmacokinetics & pharmacodynamics, small and large animal physiology, and experimental pathology, with the goal of accelerating the development of regenerative and biologically based therapies. The successful candidate is expected to establish and maintain a vigorous, externally funded research program and to contribute to the Department’s teaching, service, and outreach missions. USC provides an exceptionally collaborative environment, with additional opportunities for interaction with the Eli and Edythe Broad Center for Regenerative Medicine, the USC Center for Advanced Computing (CARC), the Zilkha Neurogenetic Institute, the USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center, clinical departments across the Keck School of Medicine, and the Department of Quantitative and Computational Biology in the USC Dornsife College of Letters, Arts, and Sciences. The annual base salary range for this position is $160,000-$425,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. Applications should include a letter of interest; a curriculum vitae; a two- to three-page statement of past, present, and future research; and contact information for four references. All materials should be submitted by 11/30/2026 for priority consideration. USC values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20177789 Posted Date 07/30/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. L