    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-radiation-oncology-practitioner/1209/99480500128": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiation Oncology (Practitioner)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiation Oncology (Practitioner) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiation Oncology (Practitioner) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179035 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which comprises the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Radiation Oncology, Keck School of Medicine of University of Southern California is a robust team of clinicians and basic science/clinical researchers consisting of approximately 15 physician faculty and 10 medical physicist faculty. We provide services at seven hospitals, including Keck Hospital of USC, Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center, Children’s Hospital of Los Angeles, USC Arcadia Hospital, Henry Mayo Newall Hospital and five community-based clinics. The Department has ACR accreditation for USC Norris Cancer Hospital and its Keck Medicine of USC regional radiation oncology clinics. The CHLA radiation oncology unit has earned APEX accreditation and is part of the USC/Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center, an NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center. The program is a full member of the NRG, NSABP, and GOG. It also participates in clinical trials sponsored by SWOG. Our medical physics faculty are directly involved in ensuring quality and safety for clinical operations, clinical research, and education and are maintain a CAMPEP accredited medical physics residency training program. The Department at the USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center is equipped with a Varian Truebeam STX with Brain Lab ExacTrac for high precision monitoring of positioning during treatment, a Varian Truebeam with HyperArc, and a Trilogy machine. Additional integrated technologies include a dedicated Siemens CT simulator, Varian RPM respiratory gating, and prone breast technique. The HDR brachytherapy program is housed in a dedicated procedural suite with full anesthesia capability, and Bravos HDR brachytherapy unit and is active in GU, GYN, skin cancers with plans to add other disease sites. The Keck Hospital houses a new Gamma knife Espirit. . An ongoing program in ocular melanoma involves joint faculty from the Roski Eye Institute who treat patients with episcleral plaque brachytherapy. The department’s community-based clinics feature new Varian Truebeam and Halcyon (ring-based gantry) linear accelerators with capabilities for gating, radiosurgery and SBRT. Position Summary The Department of Radiation Oncology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California (USC) is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible Radiation Oncologist to join our faculty at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate will receive an academic appointment at a rank commensurate with their qualifications, training, and experience. This position offers the opportunity to practice in two thriving regional cancer programs within the Keck Medicine of USC network: the Keck Medicine/Henry Mayo Cancer Program in Santa Clarita and the Keck Medicine Arcadia, multispecialty clinics located adjacent to USC Arcadia Hospital. The successful candidate will serve as the one of two Radiation Oncologist at both sites, working closely with multidisciplinary teams to provide exceptional, patient-centered cancer care. In addition to their primary clinical responsibilities, the faculty member will participate in providing clinical coverage at other Keck Medicine community radiation oncology practices throughout the Los Angeles and Orange County regions as needed. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to the department's primary mission of excellence in clinical care while practicing within a growing, integrated academic health system. Minimum Qualifications Board Certified/Board Eligible Physician (MD or DO); California Medical License, ABR certification or progression Graduate of a United States ACGME accredited 4-yr residency program in Radiation Oncology Possess a California Fluoroscopic supervisor’s license Radiation Oncology experience in an academic medical center satellite or community setting Preferred Qualifications The ideal faculty candidate should possess excellent leadership skills in a community-based radiation oncology setting, familiarity with community-based health care, rich experience in oncology practice and operations, and ability to promote a culture of quality and safety. Exempt Position We offer a highly competitive salary package with excellent benefits ( https://employees.usc.edu/benefits-perks/ ).  Compensation will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. The annual base salary range for this position is $340,000 - $380,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations.” USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or in need of a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources at (213) 821-8100 or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. Job ID REQ20179035 Posted Date 08/20/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from t