    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-professor-of-pediatrics-clinician-educator-division-of-neonatology-chla/1209/99411019824": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Neonatology -CHLA",
      "description": "Clinical Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Neonatology -CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Neonatology -CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20179025 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Keck School of Medicine (KSOM) of the University of Southern California (USC) and Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) in the Department of Pediatrics in the Division of Neonatology are actively seeking a full-time faculty member at the rank of Clinical Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician-Educator Track). Applicants must have an MD or equivalent degree and demonstrate excellence in clinical care, education, and scholarly activities. Candidates must be board certified in Pediatrics, board certified or board eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine, and eligible for medical licensure in the State of California. The selected candidate will provide patient care in our Fetal and Neonatal Institute and its 58-bed, Level IV Newborn and Infant Critical Care Unit (NICCU) at CHLA and in our community-based NICU, site of our Fetal Maternal Center. The candidate will participate in the education and mentorship of pediatric residents and neonatal-perinatal fellows. Our program sponsors its own ACGME-accredited Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine Fellowship. The selected candidate will join a nationally recognized division of pediatric neonatologists and advanced practice providers with expertise spanning a broad range of neonatal and perinatal conditions. This position offers excellent opportunities for teaching, mentorship, scholarly activities, quality improvement, and participation in collaborative research initiatives through Children's Hospital Los Angeles and USC. The Fetal and Neonatal Institute consists of the CHLA Division of Neonatology, CHLA-USC Fetal Maternal Center, and Newborn Follow-Up Program. The CHLA-USC Fetal Maternal Center is one of the largest fetal diagnosis and fetal intervention centers in the nation. The annual base salary range for this position is $158,177-$517,500. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations Children’s Hospital Los Angeles is ranked among the top hospitals in the nation for neonatology on the U.S. News & World Report Best Children's Hospitals List. We are a recognized leader in state-of-the-art evaluation, diagnosis and treatment for all newborns and infants with complex medical and surgical conditions. The Fetal and Neonatal Institute offers multidisciplinary care supported by nationally recognized subspecialists across all major pediatric disciplines. If interested, please apply using the link above. For further inquiries, please contact: Philippe S. Friedlich, M.D., MS Epi, MBA Teresa and Byron Pollitt Family Chair in Fetal & Neonatal Medicine Professor of Pediatrics & Surgery, USC Keck School of Medicine Co-Director, Fetal and Neonatal Institute Chief, Division of Neonatology Children's Hospital Los Angeles E-mail: pfriedlich@chla.usc.edu We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or in need of a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources at (213) 821-8100 or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. Job ID REQ20179025 Posted Date 08/18/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Tro