    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-research-orthopaedic-surgery-chla/1209/99216247632": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Research Orthopaedic Surgery CHLA",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Research Orthopaedic Surgery CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Research Orthopaedic Surgery CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178881 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Keck School of Medicine (KSOM) of the University of Southern California (USC) and Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) are actively seeking a full-time faculty member for the position of Assistant Professor of Research Orthopedic Surgery to join the Division of Orthopedic Surgery at CHLA and the Department of Orthopedic Surgery at KSOM of USC. The successful candidate will join 15 other full-time faculty members in the Jackie and Gene Autry Orthopedic Center at Children’s Hospital Los Angeles. Primary responsibilities include: Conduct, publish, and obtain funding for original research in clinical motion analysis and biomechanics Oversee all research in the CHLA Motion and Sports Analysis Laboratory Promote and expand the reputation of the Motion Lab’s research program within the motion analysis and biomechanics communities Supervise and mentor students, research staff, and research volunteers Contribute to process and technical advancements in the Motion Lab A competitive salary and benefits package will be offered. Applicant requirements include a PhD in Kinesiology, Biomedical Engineering, or related field; at least 5 years’ experience in human motion analysis; and experience with Vicon and Qualisys motion analysis systems preferred. CHLA is the largest and most comprehensive pediatric hospital in the Los Angeles area. The Jackie and Gene Autry Orthopedic Center also features the renowned John C. Wilson, Jr. Motion Analysis Laboratory, a source of outstanding clinical care and research. The orthopedic center is consistently ranked in the Top 5 nationally by U.S. News and World Report. USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. The annual base salary range for this position is $130,000-$140,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or in need of a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources at (213) 821-8100 or by email at uschr@usc.edu. Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. If interested, please apply using the link above. For further inquiries, please contact: Robert Kay, MD Medical Director, Jackie and Gene Autry Orthopedic Center Division Chief, Orthopaedic Surgery Director, Neuromuscular Program RKay@chla.usc.edu Job ID REQ20178881 Posted Date 08/14/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 202