    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-clinical-medicine-division-of-endocrinology/1209/99128022240": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine (Division of Endocrinology)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine (Division of Endocrinology) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine (Division of Endocrinology) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177746 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Medicine at the Keck School of Medicine is seeking an outstanding full-time General Endocrinologist to join the Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes as an Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine. Position Overview The successful candidate will provide high-quality clinical care across the spectrum of general endocrinology and will play an active role in teaching Endocrinology fellows, Internal Medicine residents, and medical students. This position offers the opportunity to practice in a dynamic academic medical center serving a diverse patient population. Qualifications • Board certified in Internal Medicine • Board certified or board eligible in Endocrinology, Diabetes, and Metabolism • Eligible for medical licensure in the state of California • Demonstrated excellence in clinical care • Commitment to working with diverse patients and learners What We Offer • Competitive salary package and excellent benefits • Academic appointment at the Assistant Professor level • Collaborative environment with opportunities for clinical, teaching, and scholarly growth • Supportive multidisciplinary team and access to extensive USC resources Annual base salary for this position is $200,000–$230,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups are encouraged to apply. How to Apply Please submit: • Curriculum Vitae • Cover Letter • Names and contact information for three references Send materials to: Roxanne Odom: Division of Endocrinology and Diabetes Email: rodrom@usc.edu Job ID REQ20177746 Posted Date 08/12/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in