      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Orthopaedic Surgery (Sports Medicine) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Clinical Orthopaedic Surgery (Sports Medicine) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177737 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. Sports Medicine Physician Department of Orthopaedic Surgery The Department of Orthopaedic Surgery at the Keck Medical Center of USC is seeking an orthopaedic surgeon specializing in Sports Medicine surgery to join our expanding clinical practice in Los Angeles, CA. This position provides an outstanding opportunity for an individual with excellent clinical skills and an interest in teaching, research, and team coverage. A faculty appointment at a level appropriate to experience and training is available at the Keck School of Medicine of USC. The annual base salary range for this position is $350,000-$400,000.  When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Please apply here. For further inquiries please contact: Jay R. Lieberman, M.D. Chair, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery Keck Medical Center of USC Attn: Wendy Fang 1540 Alcazar St. CHP 207, Los Angeles, CA 90089. Wendy.fang@med.usc.edu Job ID REQ20177737 Posted Date 08/12/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 