    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-instructor-of-family-medicine-practitioner-street-medicine/1209/98907589648": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Family Medicine (Practitioner) Street Medicine",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor of Family Medicine (Practitioner) Street Medicine at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructor of Family Medicine (Practitioner) Street Medicine Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178615 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Family Medicine of the Keck School of Medicine of USC provides care for every member of the family, across generations and over lifetimes. We aim to enhance the quality of life for underserved and vulnerable patients while educating future generations of highly skilled, compassionate primary care specialists. Our goal is to combine education, patient advocacy, and evidence-based research to advance family medicine and geriatrics. USC Street Medicine is hiring a full-time Advanced Practice Provider (APP), Clinical Instructor of Family Medicine (Practitioner), to deliver care directly to patients experiencing homelessness in their own environments—under bridges, in encampments, and on the street. This is a unique opportunity to help advance the field of street medicine in Los Angeles, home to the largest unsheltered homeless population in the United States. As part of a multidisciplinary team, the APP will provide diagnostic, therapeutic, preventive, and health maintenance services under the direction and supervision of a licensed physician. City of Los Angeles Neighborhood Primary Care Teams USC Street Medicine operates 6 Neighborhood Primary Care Teams in the City of Los Angeles: Eastside, Central, South LA, Mid-City, Hollywood and MacArthur Park.  Each interprofessional Neighborhood Primary Care Team includes an Advanced Practice Provider, Community Health Worker and nursing support. This team will deliver comprehensive care addressing physical health, mental health, and substance use disorders for individuals experiencing unsheltered homelessness in the service area. Team members will also be supported by USC Street Medicine’s broader system of care, including HIV Medicine, Women’s Health, Addiction Medicine, Psychiatry, Behavioral Health Therapy, Social Work and Enhanced Care Management. Although this is a Clinical Faculty position on the “Practitioner” track, there will also be opportunities to teach Physician Assistant students, medical students, Family Medicine residents, and other learners during street-based rounds. This is a unique opportunity to provide high-quality healthcare to patients with complex physical and behavioral health needs, supported by an experienced team of street medicine clinicians. This is a full-time, exempt, in-person position based in Los Angeles, CA, with work conducted in the field. This role does not offer a hybrid or remote schedule. The schedule is Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–4:00 p.m. Required Education: current Advanced Practitioner License (PA, NP, etc.) Preferred Experience: 3 years, experience working with the homeless population, experience with treatment of Substance Use Disorders, experience with Primary Care and Mental Health treatments The annual base salary range for this position is $135,000 - $150,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20178615 Posted Date 08/07/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - 