    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-clinical-obstetrics-and-gynecology/1209/98860067104": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178169 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology  - Division of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Gynecologic Sub-Specialties Job Description The University of Southern California (USC) was founded in 1880 and is the largest private employer in the city of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is composed of the faculty, students and staff at USC. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Keck School of Medicine of USC is seeking an Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology to serve as a full-time Gynecology physician at our USC Verdugo Hills outpatient clinic and hospital.  The faculty position would be a part of the Division of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Gynecologic Sub-Specialties. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is also committed to serving the underserved population in East Los Angeles through our affiliation with Los Angeles General Medical Center (formerly known as LAC+USC). Clinical responsibilities will include outpatient and surgical care of gynecology patients: Preventive Care & Screenings :  Conducting annual well-woman exams, breast exams, and cervical cancer screenings as needed Sexual & Reproductive Health : Diagnosing and treating sexually transmitted infections (STIs), menstrual disorders, and pelvic pain. Family Planning : Advising on birth control options, managing contraception, and assessing fertility concerns. Menopause management : Diagnosis, evaluation and symptom management such as hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT) and non-hormonal medications Gynecologic Surgery : Performing both minimally invasive and complex Scope of Work : Supervise a nurse practitioner in clinic; Perform thorough medical history and physical; timely completion of detailed and accurate documentation of assessment, including updated problem lists and care plans for each patient encounter; complete orders and perform appropriate tests analysis, and diagnostic procedures as required and recommended by an evidence-based practice; administer and prescribe appropriate treatments and medications; minimum daily patient threshold Qualifications: MD degree with completion of a 4-year ACGME accredited Ob/Gyn residency Board Certified i Obstetrics and Gynecology The successful candidate is expected to apply for a CA medical license and be licensed to practice medicine in California by the time of appointment. The position offers a salary with excellent university benefits and an academic appointment at the Keck School of Medicine of USC commensurate with the level of training and experience.  The annual base salary for this position is $260,000-$290,000 , which is negotiable based on qualifications and experience. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Qualified candidates should respond with a letter of interest, CV, and three recommendation letters to Rizalyn Reynaldo, EdD (rizalyna.reynaldo@med.usc.edu), Chief Administrative Officer in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Recommendations letters should be addressed to Dr. Joseph Ouzounian, Daniel R. Mishell Jr. MD Endowed Professor and Chair, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Job ID REQ20178169 Posted Date 08/06/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture &