    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/full-time-teaching-track-faculty-positions-in-biological-sciences/1209/98854765984": {
      "title": "Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Positions in Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Positions in Biological Sciences at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Full-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Positions in Biological Sciences Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20178480 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Departments of Marine and Environmental Biology, Molecular and Cellular Biosciences, Neurobiology and Human and Evolutionary Biology in the Dana and David Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences at the University of Southern California in Los Angeles, California, seeks applications for full-time, teaching-track instructor positions for the 2026-2027 academic year. We seek instructors who have experience in teaching undergraduate laboratories in one or more of the following subject areas: General Biology, Biochemistry, Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Neurobiology and Physiology. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in a relevant field, e.g. Biology, Biochemistry, Chemistry, Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Neurobiology or Physiology with demonstrated teaching experience in one of these areas. Please submit a cover letter, CV, verified teaching evaluation scores for at least two years and the names of three referees who may be contacted by USC for letters of reference that speak to your teaching abilities. Applications will be reviewed immediately and continue until the position is filled. In order to be considered for this position, all candidates must apply via the \"Apply\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The annual base salary range for this position is $80,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations Job ID REQ20178480 Posted Date 08/06/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC 