    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/associate-or-assistant-professor-of-clinical-obstetrics-and-gynecology-minimally-invasive-gynecolog/1209/98098212960": {
      "title": "Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology- Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgeon",
      "description": "Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology- Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgeon at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Obstetrics and Gynecology- Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgeon Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177821 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC) was founded in 1880 and is the largest private employer in the city of Los Angeles.  The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California is seeking a fellowship trained, board certified, academic Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgeon at the level of assistant or associate professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology.  This position is ideally suited to a mid-career faculty member. The faculty position would be a part of the Division of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Gynecologic Sub-Specialties and would practice at Keck Medical Center of USC and our affiliated hospitals.  The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is also committed to serving the underserved population in East Los Angeles through our affiliation with Los Angeles General Medical Center (formerly known as LAC+USC). We are seeking a highly motivated individual who has demonstrated clinical excellence and whose primary responsibility will be to develop the Keck Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgery practice, including outreach and shaping service-line growth (clinical protocols, referral relationships, education/outreach). This physician must also have dedication for teaching and training future gynecologists. Clinical responsibilities will include the outpatient and surgical care of complex patients: Perform advanced hysteroscopic, laparoscopic, and robotic procedures (e.g., advanced hysterectomy, myomectomy, excision of endometriosis, lysis of adhesions, adnexal surgery) Office-based procedures and evidence-based medical management Consults and longitudinal care for fibroids, endometriosis, pelvic pain, AUB, and other benign GYN conditions Collaborate on care pathways, ERAS protocols, and quality improvement initiatives The research responsibilities of this position include traditional scholarship that is required for an academic promotion, including conducting and assisting in research projects, and mentoring trainees. Qualifications: MD degree with completion of a 4-year ACGME accredited Ob/Gyn residency Board Certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology Must have completed a fellowship in Minimally Invasive Gynecology Surgery The successful candidate is expected to apply for a CA medical license and be licensed to practice medicine in California by the time of appointment. Comfort with advanced laparoscopy and robotic surgery (da Vinci) The position offers a salary with excellent university benefits and an academic appointment at the Keck School of Medicine of USC commensurate with the level of training and experience. The annual base salary for this position is $290,000-$325,000, which is negotiable based on qualifications and experience. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Qualified candidates should respond with a letter of interest, CV, and three recommendation letters to Rizalyn Reynaldo, EdD (rizalyna.reynaldo@med.usc.edu), Chief Administrative Officer in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Recommendations letters should be addressed to Dr. Joseph Ouzounian, Daniel R. Mishell Jr. MD Endowed Professor and Chair, Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Job ID REQ20177821 Posted Date 07/21/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team update