    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-associate-assistant-professor-of-medical-education-clinician-educator/1209/96857551248": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate/Assistant Professor of Medical Education (Clinician Educator)",
      "description": "Clinical Associate/Assistant Professor of Medical Education (Clinician Educator) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Associate/Assistant Professor of Medical Education (Clinician Educator) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20175825 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Department: Medical Education Program: Doctor of Medicine (MD) Program Reports To: Associate Dean for Curriculum and Educational Strategy Position Summary The Director of Assessment and Evaluation oversees the planning, implementation, analysis, and continuous improvement of assessment and evaluation processes within the MD program. This role ensures the integrity, accuracy, and effectiveness of course, clerkship, faculty, and program-level evaluations, supporting data-driven decision-making and compliance with accreditation standards. The Director of Assessment and Evaluation works collaboratively with faculty, course/clerkship directors, curriculum leaders, institutional research teams, and administrative staff to maintain high-quality assessment and evaluation systems that promote educational excellence and continuous quality improvement. Key Responsibilities 1. Evaluation System Management Lead the administration and maintenance of assessment and evaluation tools. Manage electronic assessment and evaluation platforms and ensure optimal system functionality. Oversee evaluation schedules, deployment, response monitoring, and follow-up processes. 2. Data Analysis & Reporting Analyze quantitative and qualitative evaluation data. Develop dashboards, summary reports, and trend analyses for leadership and committees. Identify patterns, strengths, and areas for improvement within courses and clerkships. Present findings to senior leadership. 3. Accreditation & Compliance Support preparation of accreditation reports and documentation. Maintain records and documentation required for internal and external review. 4. Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) Monitor effectiveness of changes and track longitudinal outcomes. Contribute to annual program evaluation reports. 5. Faculty & Staff Support Provide training to faculty and staff on evaluation tools 6. Policy & Process Development Adhere to policies related to student assessment and evaluations, faculty evaluations, and program review processes. Ensure compliance with FERPA and institutional data governance policies. 7. Collaboration & Leadership Serve as a key member of the Office of Medical Education team. Participate in curriculum committees and subcommittees. Qualifications Required PhD in education, educational measurement, public health, health professions education, statistics, or related field. 3–5 years of experience in program evaluation, higher education administration, or medical education. Experience with survey and evaluation platforms (e.g., Qualtrics, MedHub, E*Value, New Innovations). Strong analytical skills, including experience with data analysis software (e.g., Excel, SPSS, R, Tableau, or similar). Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Experience in undergraduate medical education. Experience developing dashboards or data visualization tools. Core Competencies Analytical and critical thinking Attention to detail Project management Data integrity and confidentiality Interpersonal and collaborative skills Continuous improvement mindset Ability to manage multiple deadlines Salary Range 100,000-120,000. This position is in house, Located in the Keith Administration Building of the Keck School of Medicine -Los Angeles, CA USC values diversity and is committee to equal opportunity employment. Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20175825 Posted Date 06/24/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Faculty Development Genetics Grants Administration & Sponsored Programs Health and Medical Services Human Resources Information Technology Information Technology Services Institutional Research and Planning Keck Medicine of USC Laboratory Laboratory and Research Marketing and Events Nursing Nursing Services Pharmacy Physician Assistant Postdoctoral Public Safety Radio Broadcast Research and Clinical Support Research and Grants Administration Social Work Speech Therapy Student Support Services Support Services Technician Therapy and Rehabilitation USC Job Families School/Division Select One Keck Medicine of USC Keck School of Medicine Auxiliary Services Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences Sol Price School of Public Policy Gould School of Law Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry Marshall School of Business Viterbi School of Engineering University Relations USC Credit Union Alfred E. Mann School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences Enrollment Services Facilities Management Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance School of Architecture Keck School of Medicine of USC Administrative Operations Annenberg School for Communication and Journalism Capital Construction Dworak-Peck School of Social Work Financial and Business Services Information Technology Services SOWK USC Keck School of Medicine University Advancement Bovard College Communications Iovine and Young Academy Leonard Davis School of Gerontology Office of Research Office of the Provost Rossier School of Education At USC Arcadia Hospital every team member of our 348-bed hospital strives to provide an exceptional patient experience while Athletics Facilities Planning and Management Kaufman School of Dance Keck School Of Medicine Libraries President Roski School of Art and Design School of Cinemati