    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/pt-adjunct-lecturer/1209/98432271728": {
      "title": "PT Adjunct Lecturer",
      "description": "PT Adjunct Lecturer at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs PT Adjunct Lecturer Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20175523 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is located in the heart of downtown Los Angeles and is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. USC is consistently ranked among the nation’s most prestigious universities, and the USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology features one of the world’s best degree and research programs in gerontology. The USC Leonard Davis School of Gerontology has an international reputation as a hub of aging research and with additional strong programs throughout the university, leads the way in defining and advancing the field of gerontology: https://gero.usc.edu The Leonard Davis School of Gerontology and Andrus Gerontology Center are multidisciplinary in their research and curriculum goals. This recruiting effort seeks candidates from diverse backgrounds and cultures, including graduates in disciplines and professions such as epidemiology, neuropsychology, and health services. Additionally, opportunities are available for joint appointments with academic units across the USC Campus. Cluster hires in areas of interest are possible. We are in search of Three Part-Time Lecturers or Adjunct Instructors specializing in aging-related services. Position 1: Lecturer or Adjunct Instructor – Financial Gerontology (GERO 452) Focus: Economics and the Aged We are seeking an expert in Financial Gerontology to lead GERO 452: Economics and the Aged. The ideal candidate will possess a multidisciplinary background that intersects the financial, legal, and psychological aspects of aging. Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in financial planning, economics, and law as they relate to the aging population. Key Responsibilities: Deliver curriculum covering economic policy, retirement security, and legal protections for older adults. Experience: Previous teaching experience is strongly preferred. Demonstrated history of working directly with or on behalf of older adults. Familiarity with academic accreditation a plus. Position 2 and 3: Adjunct Instructor – Senior Living Leadership Focus: Senior Living Industry Development and operations. We are in search of a seasoned leader from the Senior Living Industry to provide students with high-level operational insights. This role requires a professional who bridges the gap between executive leadership and classroom instruction. Qualifications: Must hold an MBA , MSG or equivalent advanced degree. A deep understanding of how aging services can be leveraged to benefit older adults across senior living communities. Key Attributes: Strong business acumen and a vast professional network of industry associates to engage as guest lecturers. Translating industry experience into actionable lessons on service delivery and organizational growth Experience: Extensive leadership experience in senior living environments and a background in post-secondary teaching. Must be able to teach any of the following courses: GERO 501 - Applied Legal and Regulatory Issues in Aging GERO 502 - Marketing and Shifts in Consumer Decision Making GERO 504 - Current Issues in Aging Services Management GERO 574 - Leadership and Management in Senior Living GERO 578 - Revenue Management for Senior Living GERO 589 - Case Studies in Leadership and Change Management GERO 552 - Human Resources and Aging GERO 504 - Current Issues in Aging Services Management Successful candidates should be subject matter experts in one or more of the following:  Business development and operations in the senior living and healthcare markets. Must have expertise in development, finance, operations, marketing, branding. Part-Time and Adjunct Lecturers spend most of their time on teaching and teaching-related duties and may also assist in the development of our new courses as well as the development of new curricula and accreditation, as needed. USC reserves the “Adjunct Lecturer” appointment for faculty teaching less than full-time at USC who are employed full-time in a primary profession or career elsewhere. Adjunct faculty may teach one class each semester (summer, fall, and spring). USC reserves the “Part-Time Lecturer” appointment for faculty teaching less than full-time who are not employed full-time in a primary position or career elsewhere. Part-Time Lecturers are eligible to teach more than one course a semester. These are part-time roles that will require substantial commitment and flexibility. Instructors are required to teach in person (on–campus) and to have regular office hours to assist our students. Preferred Qualifications for all Positions Graduate degree or 15+ years of experience in senior living field Experience with distance learning Prior teaching experience at the university level Prior course development experience Qualifications: A MBA or MSG degree or equivalent degree is required, and a minimum of 5 years of combined professional and teaching experience is preferred. Preference is given to candidates with a proven track record of prior teaching experience at a recognized university, and the ability to teach courses focused on business development, operations (including human resources), marketing and branding. The core salary range for this position is $38 - $42 per hour. These are part-time roles with effort below 50%. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, as well as external market and organizational considerations. In order to be considered for this position, all candidates must apply via the \"Apply\" link at the top or bottom of this page. Qualified applicants should submit a cover letter, C.V.,  and teaching statements, and the contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Job ID REQ20175523 Posted Date 07/28/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Support Coordinator II - Beach Cities Ortho Manhattan Beach - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Manhattan Beach, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Postdoctoral Scholar - Research Associate Los Angeles, California Save Job Instructor of Clinical Physical Therapy (Keck Hospital) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Divi