      "title": "Primary Care Physician APP (PA, NP):Family Medicine",
      "description": "Primary Care Physician APP (PA, NP):Family Medicine at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Primary Care Physician APP (PA, NP):Family Medicine Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20175905 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\". Faculty, students, staff, and alumni cultivate a deep commitment to each other and the university’s impact. Primary Care-APP, Clinical Instructor of Family Medicine (Clinician Practitioner) The Department of Family Medicine at Keck School of Medicine of USC is seeking a faculty physician to join our Academic Primary Care Practice in Los Angeles County. We are looking for candidates committed to providing exceptional, comprehensive, patient-centered care across the lifespan. About Us Keck Medicine of USC is a rapidly growing health system in partnership with Keck School of Medicine, recognized for delivering high-quality, compassionate, and innovative care. The Department of Family Medicine is leading the expansion of primary care services, creating models to provide care customized to meet the needs of patients and communities including street medicine, care for patients with long COVID, gender affirming care, student health and care for older adults and caregivers. We are nationally recognized for excellence Street Medicine, training students and residents in primary care.  We are deeply engaged in advancing health equity and community impact. Our Residency program is focused on training a diverse, culturally congruent healthcare workforce to be leaders in patient-centered care. We are led by a dynamic Chair and Associate Dean of Primary Care and a team of leaders who are committed to innovation, workforce development, and expanding access across Los Angeles communities Role Highlights Join our interdisciplinary care team and work alongside primary care colleagues plus partners in clinical pharmacy, behavioral health, OT/PT, and specialty care. Deliver high-quality outpatient family medicine for diverse populations. Enjoy an opportunity to teach and mentor students and residents and engage in research and quality improvement. Qualifications PA or NP from an accredited program. Board-certified or Board-eligible. Eligible for California licensure. Minimum of two years of clinical experience as a practicing primary care clinician. Strong communication skills and commitment to cultural competence and interprofessional practice. Compensation & Benefits Annual base salary: $135,000 - $170,000 commensurate with experience, with opportunity for additional compensation through incentive payment model. Comprehensive USC benefits, CME time, and faculty development support. USC values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. Should we say a chair and committed team of leaders? Job ID REQ20175905 Posted Date 06/04/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and