    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-pediatrics-clinician-educator-division-of-pulmonary-and-sleep-medic/1209/96522258832": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine CHLA",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator) Division of Pulmonary and Sleep Medicine CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20176488 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Keck School of Medicine (KSOM) of the University of Southern California (USC) and Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) in the Department of Pediatrics in the Division of Pulmonology and Sleep Medicine, are actively seeking a full-time faculty member for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor of Pediatrics (Clinician Educator). The Department of Pediatrics at Children's Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) and the Keck School of Medicine of University of Southern California (USC) seek a full-time faculty member for the position of Pediatric Pulmonologist with an emphasis in Sleep Medicine. The ideal candidate would have an MD or MD/PhD, be board-certified or board eligible in Pediatric Pulmonology as well as sleep medicine, and qualify for a USC faculty appointment at the Assistant Professor level. The Division of Pediatric Pulmonology and Sleep Medicine has fifteen full-time and one part-time faculty members. Each faculty member has a clinical and research profile that is tailored to their specific interests. The Division includes a Cystic Fibrosis Center, Pulmonary Function and Exercise Physiology Laboratory, Sleep Center, Infant Pulmonary Function Testing, Bronchoscopy Program, Home Mechanical Ventilation Program, Diaphragmatic Pacing Program, and is affiliated with a large chronic care facility. Our sleep center is accredited by the American Academy of Sleep Medicine (AASM). We perform over 2,500 polysomnographies a year and maintain a sleep disorders consultation clinic. We currently have five triple boarded sleep specialists. We have an ACGME sleep collaboration with the KSOM LAC+USC/University Hospital sleep fellowship program with two fellows per year dividing their time between the two sites. The recruited faculty member would have specific responsibilities as part of the sleep center team. The division has dedicated nurse specialists, social workers, dieticians, respiratory care practitioners, and research support staff. The Division has an ACGME accredited fellowship program with 6 post-graduate pulmonary fellows. The Pulmonology Clinic receives referrals from the entire southwestern region with almost 7,700 ambulatory patient visits per year. The Division staffs four outreach clinics as well. The Pediatric Pulmonology program has been consistently ranked in the top 11 Programs by the US News and World Report. Research in the Division is focused on cystic fibrosis, sleep and sleep related breathing disorders, home mechanical ventilation, sudden infant death syndrome, medical ethics, and pulmonary complications of hemoglobinpathies. Children's Hospital Los Angeles is top 10 Children's Hospitals in the nation and number 1 in the Pacific region in the United States in the current US News and World Report. CHLA is a freestanding, private not-for-profit children's hospital affiliated with the USC, Keck School of Medicine. CHLA completed a new in-patient hospital tower in 2011 with over 300 beds. The Saban Research Institute at CHLA provides state of the art basic science facilities in stem cell research, transplant immunology, and developmental biology. The USC KSOM was established in 1885 and has over 1,200 full time faculty members and is home to over 25 research-oriented basic and clinical academic programs. Academic appointments through USC Keck School of Medicine are available at a level appropriate to training and experience. The salary and academic rank would be commensurate with experience. Relocation expenses are provided, and the position includes generous benefits and retirement package. The annual base salary range for this position is $95,904-$325,712. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. Lara Christine Bishay, MD, MPH Chief, Pediatric Pulmonology and Sleep Medicine Children’s Hospital Los Angeles Keck School of Medicine University of Southern California lbishay@chla.usc.edu 323-361-2101 If interested, please apply using the link above. For further inquiries, please contact: Anissa Chavez (323) 361-4570 Job ID REQ20176488 Posted Date 06/16/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Research Coordinator I Los Angeles, California Save Job Support Coordinator II - Beach Cities Ortho Manhattan Beach - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Non-Exempt) (Non-Union) Manhattan Beach, California Save Job Account Receivable Collections, Lead - Patient Accounting - Full 