    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-clinical-pharmacy-teaching-track-director-of-professional-/1209/97887809488": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Clinical Pharmacy (Teaching Track) , Director of Professional Experience Programs",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Clinical Pharmacy (Teaching Track) , Director of Professional Experience Programs at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Clinical Pharmacy (Teaching Track) , Director of Professional Experience Programs Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177627 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC) Alfred E. Mann School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences (USC Mann) invites applications for a full-time, 12-month calendar, non-tenure track faculty position in the Titus Family Department of Clinical Pharmacy. The successful candidate will be appointed to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Clinical Pharmacy (Teaching Track) and will serve as the Director of Professional Experience Programs.  This position does not lead to consideration for tenure. The Teaching Track faculty position combines educational administrative leadership with teaching and mentoring responsibilities, which together comprise at least 80% of the faculty member’s assigned effort. Teaching responsibilities include coordination of Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiences (APPEs), and provision of didactic instruction in experiential related topics and courses. The remaining 20% will be dedicated to service and scholarly activities. Department, school, university, and professional service are expected. Scholarly activities are encouraged and are an important component of a well-rounded faculty candidate’s recruitment and success, and collaboration opportunities with other educational scholars are available. As a faculty member, service to the school through active participation is expected. Routine faculty administration and participation duties, such as attendance at departmental and full faculty meetings and committee service, as well as annual peer review submissions and peer-to-peer teaching evaluations are expected. The faculty member should also contribute to the growth of the profession through service on a national level. Inclusive teaching methods and expert use of pedagogical techniques and technologies are expected. The Director of Professional Experience Programs provides strategic leadership for the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of the Doctor of Pharmacy (PharmD) experiential curriculum. The successful candidate will lead the experiential education team, including the Director of Experiential Assessment, the Director of Introductory Pharmacy Practice Experience (IPPE) Programs, and the professional staff, while fostering a collaborative and high-performing work environment. The Director will work closely with USC Mann students, faculty, staff, preceptors, external partners, and affiliated organizations to ensure experiential programs meet accreditation standards, supports student success, and advances the school’s mission. The position is primarily based on the USC Health Sciences Campus, with occasional travel required for site visits, conferences, and domestic or international experiential programs. Specific responsibilities include: Provide strategic leadership and oversight for all PharmD experiential education programs. Ensure compliance with Accreditation Council for Pharmacy Education (ACPE) standards and institutional policies. Supervise experiential education faculty and staff, providing direction, mentorship, and performance oversight to support operational effectiveness and efficiency. Execute and coordinate the APPE program. Develop, implement, and evaluate preceptor recruitment, onboarding, training, recognition, and engagement initiatives. Conduct site visits to recruit, evaluate, and maintain high-quality experiential practice sites and preceptors. Oversee the development, execution, and maintenance of affiliation agreements between USC Mann and experiential practice sites. Recruit new experiential practice sites and preceptors. Provide input on hiring for experiential faculty and staff positions, as needed. Provide collaborative oversight for appointing qualified adjunct faculty preceptors. Collaborate with the Chief International Officer to support and expand international experiential education opportunities. Required Qualifications, Credentials and Experience Applicants must have a PharmD degree and California licensure (or eligibility for licensure by passing the state board exam at the first available sitting). Candidates who have completed a pharmacy residency and/or fellowship are preferred. Candidates must have prior experience in academia, including demonstrated experiential education programming leadership, assessment, teaching, precepting, and scholarship, along with proven excellence, leadership, knowledge, and skills to collaborate with partners and represent USC Mann externally. Greater demonstrated levels of academic and educational accomplishments and leadership skills are expected for those considered for the associate professor and professor ranks, commensurate with the standards used for promotion at USC. Strong leadership, written, and verbal communication skills; analytical skills with the ability to interpret and communicate complex data effectively; ability to multitask, problem solve and collaborate with other team members; and a commitment to treating all individuals with respect and dignity are required. Skills in using educational tools and technologies, such as learning management systems, data analytics software, and Microsoft Word, Excel, and PowerPoint are preferred. Description of Institution/Organization USC Mann is located on the USC Health Sciences Campus, which includes the Keck Hospital of USC and outpatient, the Norris Cancer Hospital, and Los Angeles General Medical Center, along with directing four university and community-based pharmacies, having pioneered the recent addition of the USC Pharmacy and Wellness Center in South Los Angeles – a site inclusive of planned student clinical rotations. Ranked as the #1 school of pharmacy among private schools in the country, USC Mann is recognized for its more than century-long international reputation for innovation in pharmaceutical education, practice, and research. The school uniquely spans the entire spectrum of pharmaceutical development and clinical care – from drug discovery to regulatory approaches that promote safety and innovation, from delivery of patient care services to evaluating the impact of care on patient outcomes and costs. The school's dynamic faculty contribute to a broad range of educational programs, including undergraduate majors, multiple master's and PhD programs, the Doctor of Pharmacy program with dual-degree options, and advanced clinical residency and fellowship training. Their teaching spans the full spectrum of translational education, from laboratory discovery to bedside practice.  The school has recently received a $50 million endowment from the Alfred E. Mann Foundation to name the school and to support student scholarships, faculty development and recruitment, and integrated biomedical innovation. USC is actively committed to equal opportunity within its faculty hiring practices, so all qualified candidates are encouraged to apply. Compensation and Benefits The University of Southern California offers a competitive salary within an academic environment based on the candidate’s experience and accomplishments. The University also offers excellent benefits to employees, which include health, dental and life insurance; tuition assistance; disability and retirement plans; credit union membership; and participation in cultural and social events, as well as access to athletic and recreational facilities. The position does not lead to consideration for tenure. Merit reviews are conducted annually from which salary enhancements are decided. Re-appointment and promotion within the teaching track are based on performance assessment longitudinally via administrative review, with department evaluation, dossier submission and internal/external review. The annual base salary range for this position is $140,000 - $190,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer alignment, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Application Procedure For consideration, please apply online using the following link: https://usccareers.usc.edu . Interested individuals should electronically submit a letter of intent or personal statement that includes how you will use your experience to address the responsibilities of the position, current curriculum vitae, and the names of five references with current contact information. Applicant screening will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Job ID REQ20177627 Posted Date 07/16/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs S