    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/research-assistant-professor-of-biomedical-engineering/1209/94497967904": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering",
      "description": "Research Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Research Assistant Professor of Biomedical Engineering Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174554 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The USC Viterbi School of Engineering ( http://viterbi.usc.edu ) at the University of Southern California seeks outstanding research faculty candidates for full-time, non-tenure track, benefits-eligible research positions in the Alfred E. Mann Department of Biomedical Engineering ( https://bme.usc.edu/ ). All candidates are expected to have a strong commitment to research. Research faculty are not eligible for tenure and have no obligation to teach in the Department. Appointments may be considered for up to three years, subject to renewal upon satisfactory performance and available funding. We are seeking highly qualified and motivated researchers with a Ph.D. in Biomedical Engineering or a related discipline and a minimum of four years of postdoctoral research experience. The successful candidate will possess strong technical and analytical skills in either of the following areas: Ultrasound and cellular and molecular bioengineering, with demonstrated ability to conduct innovative, independent research and contribute to collaborative projects. Areas of expertise should include sonogenetics, cellular and molecular engineering, genetically encoded reporter development, mechanobiology of cells within their microenvironment, and immunoengineering. Ultrasound imaging and devices, with demonstrated ability to conduct innovative, independent research and contribute to collaborative projects. Areas of expertise should include contrast-free super-resolution microvessel imaging algorithm, ultrafast ultrasound imaging system design, and hardware acceleration for real-time ultrafast ultrasound processing. Applicants should demonstrate the ability to lead and mentor multidisciplinary teams of graduate students, and a proven track record in grant proposal development and participation as Key or Senior Personnel on funded projects. Applications must include a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a concise statement of current and future research directions and funding, and names of at least three professional references. We would like to fill the position during the Summer of 2026 with a start date of July 1, 2026 or during the Spring of 2027 with a start date of January 1, 2027. Applications submitted after May 8th, 2026, may not be considered. Early application is highly encouraged. The core salary range for the positions is $85,000 - $120,000 per year. These are 12-month full-time positions. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope of responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. USC will consider for employment all qualified applicants with criminal records in a manner consistent with applicable laws and regulations, including the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for employers and the Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, and with due consideration for patient and student safety. Please refer to the Background Screening Policy Appendix D for specific employment screen implications for the position for which you are applying. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources by phone at (213) 821-8100, or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. . Job ID REQ20174554 Posted Date 04/28/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don