      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of Real Estate Careers Preparation",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor of Real Estate Careers Preparation at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Adjunct Instructor of Real Estate Careers Preparation Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174502 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) University of Southern California Sol Price School of Public Policy Adjunct Instructor of Real Estate Careers Preparation Department of Real Estate Development The USC Sol Price School of Public Policy is seeking a working professional with expertise and a primary position in commercial real estate careers preparation. The successful candidate will be able to teach an undergraduate-level course on career assessment and planning; an overview of the commercial real estate industry and career path options; and professional development skills. Minimum requirements: Advanced degree (such as MS Human Resources, MBA, MRED) preferred. Candidates without a graduate degree may be considered with a minimum of 10 years of professional experience in human resources at commercial real estate firms engaged in institutional quality transactions. The candidate must also have significant professional experience in commercial real estate human resources. Preference given to candidates with prior teaching experience and excellent teaching evaluations. Adjunct instructor responsibilities include delivery of course content, scheduling office hours and being accessible to students as appropriate, and grading. Each instructor is expected to provide students with a syllabus outlining the course goals, schedule, and all requirements for the course under the direction of the Department Chair. The USC Sol Price School of Public Policy Ranked among the foremost schools of public policy in the nation, the USC Sol Price School of Public Policy generates uncommon knowledge for the common good. The school is composed of overlapping disciplines that generate innovative approaches to critical issues ranging from health-care policy to homelessness, and sustainability to congestion – to name a few. A wide-ranging curriculum, including extensive experiential learning, prepares our graduates to navigate problems that demand multi-layered solutions driven by critical, informed thinking. The Price School, founded in 1929, is anchored by four departments: Public Policy and Management, Health Policy and Management, Wilbur H. Smith III Department of Real Estate Development, and Urban Planning and Spatial Analysis. The School’s rigorous academic programs provide students with the knowledge and distinctive opportunities to make meaningful contributions to their professions. Integrating classroom instruction with real-world experience and led by some of the world’s most renowned faculty in their fields, our students establish a clear pathway to successful careers. Our academic programs are augmented by numerous research centers, institutes and initiatives that provide additional research expertise and experiences, notable among them are: The Judith and John 