    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-instructor-of-urology-practitioner/1209/97460180304": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Urology (Practitioner)",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor of Urology (Practitioner) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructor of Urology (Practitioner) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177353 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is one of the world’s leading private research universities and the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As a member of the USC community, you will join the renowned Trojan Family—faculty, students, and staff dedicated to excellence in education, research, patient care, and service. The Department of Urology at the Keck School of Medicine of USC is seeking applicants for a Clinical Instructor of Urology (Practitioner). The Clinical Instructor of Urology (Practitioner) will provide high-quality patient care in collaboration with faculty physicians and multidisciplinary healthcare teams. Responsibilities include developing and implementing patient management plans; coordinating referrals to specialty, ancillary, and social services; documenting patient encounters and progress notes; and ensuring continuity of care. The successful candidate will perform and/or interpret common laboratory, radiologic, and other diagnostic studies used in the evaluation and management of urologic conditions. Additional duties include assisting attending physicians with a variety of urologic procedures and participating in clinical education activities appropriate to the clinician-educator role. The position offers a competitive salary, comprehensive university benefits, and an academic appointment in the Keck School of Medicine of USC commensurate with qualifications, training, and experience. The annual base salary range for this position is $225,325. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20177353 Posted Date 07/07/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page 