    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-clinical-otolaryngology-head-and-neck-surgery/1209/97241435792": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Otolaryngology Head and Neck Surgery",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Otolaryngology Head and Neck Surgery at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Clinical Otolaryngology Head and Neck Surgery Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20177129 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Faculty Position in the Division of Sleep Surgery Caruso Department of Otolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery University of Southern California, Los Angeles, California The USC Caruso Department of Otolaryngology Head and Neck Surgery seeks a board-eligible or board-certified Otolaryngologist with fellowship training and expertise in Sleep Surgery, or both Sleep Medicine and Sleep Surgery, to join our department. We are seeking an innovative clinician-scholar with demonstrated expertise or strong potential in sleep surgery, including contemporary approaches to the surgical management of obstructive sleep apnea and related sleep disorders. We seek faculty members whose career goals include excellence in patient care, research, and clinical teaching. Clinical responsibilities will include the evaluation and treatment of adult patients with sleep-related breathing disorders, including the performance of advanced sleep surgery procedures. This physician will closely collaborate with Sleep Medicine physicians and participate in the USC Multidisciplinary Sleep Center. Clinical duties will involve seeing patients in our various USC clinics, with surgery performed at Keck Medical Center of USC and other USC-affiliated hospitals. There is a strong opportunity to start a fellowship program if the candidate desires. Our institution offers tremendous clinical, research, and educational opportunities, and we encourage faculty to take full advantage of them. The department prioritizes mentorship, collaboration, and teamwork to promote faculty development within a supportive, intellectually curious, and collegial environment. Faculty are expected to pursue scholarly activities that advance patient care and contribute to the field of otolaryngology–head and neck surgery. Opportunities exist to participate in clinical research, resident and medical student education, and multidisciplinary collaborations across the USC health system. Faculty rank will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the selected candidate. The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is one of the world's leading private research universities and the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As a member of the USC faculty, you will join a distinguished academic community dedicated to advancing discovery, education, and patient care. The annual base salary range for an entry-level rank is $330,000 – $350,000. Supplemental incentive compensation will be added in accordance with the departmental compensation plan. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate's experience, education, and training, key skills, internal equity, applicable laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, and external market considerations. Job ID REQ20177129 Posted Date 07/02/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger