    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/glendale/clinical-assistant-professor-of-emergency-medicine-clinician-educator/1209/96569783984": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Emergency Medicine (Clinician Educator)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Emergency Medicine (Clinician Educator) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Emergency Medicine (Clinician Educator) Glendale, Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20176061 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles.  As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the “Trojan Family”, which is comprised of the faculty, students, and staff that make the university what it is. Keck School of Medicine’s Department of Emergency Medicine of the University of Southern California is looking to recruit a part-time Clinical Assistant Professor of Emergency Medicine (Clinician Educator) to join the department.  The candidate for this position should be board-certified or board-eligible in emergency medicine and demonstrate excellence in training and patient care.  This position offers a competitive salary, with university benefits and an academic appointment at USC’s Keck School of Medicine appropriate to the level of training and experience. The annual base salary range for this position is $290,000-$300,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations The department promotes further training in Emergency Medicine Divisions to prepare fellows/residents for future endeavors.  This position will act as a liaison, working regular shifts in the Emergency Room and bedside teaching. Job ID REQ20176061 Posted Date 06/17/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highli