    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-clinical-pathology-open-rank-division-of-transfusion-medicine/1209/94611454496": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology (Open Rank)(Division of Transfusion Medicine )",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology (Open Rank)(Division of Transfusion Medicine ) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology (Open Rank)(Division of Transfusion Medicine ) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174271 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine of the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California invites applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Division of Transfusion Medicine. Faculty members in Transfusion Medicine provide clinical service to three hospitals located on the Health Science Campus (Keck Hospital, Norris Cancer Hospital, and Los Angeles General Medical Center) and participate in teaching in the medical school and residency/fellowship programs associated with an academic medical center.  Candidates should have a demonstrated commitment to teaching and clinical service. Candidates for appointment must hold an M.D. or D.O. degree, be eligible for a California Medical license, be certified in Clinical Pathology and be certified or board eligible in Transfusion Medicine.  Interest in general laboratory medicine along with hemostasis and the diagnosis and management of coagulopathies is desirable. The annual base salary range for this position is $250,000-$450,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market as external market and organizational considerations. The position is Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor in the clinical or clinician educator tracks.  Academic rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications. Interested candidates should apply online utilizing the following link and submit their curriculum vitae, a minimum of four academic references and a synopsis of recent activities. USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources by phone at (213) 821-8100, or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law. . Job ID REQ20174271 Posted Date 05/01/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Pro