    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/associate-or-assistant-professor-of-clinical-medicine-division-of-hematology/1209/92467417120": {
      "title": "Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine Division of Hematology",
      "description": "Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine Division of Hematology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Associate or Assistant Professor of Clinical Medicine Division of Hematology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20172412 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is located in the heart of downtown L.A. and is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. Supported by a $58 million endowment, the Jane Anne Nohl Division of Hematol­ogy and Center for the Study of Blood Diseases at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California and USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center seeks faculty members interested in malignant/non-malignant Hematology, basic and translational clinical research in the area of adoptive cellular therapy, including CAR-T and TCR gene therapy. The Division has an active next generation CAR-T cell program which is expected to enter clinical testing in the near future. Candidates with experience in cGMP manufacturing of cellular therapy products and FDA IND process are strongly encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to applicants who have MD or MD/PhD degrees, BC/BE in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology and eligibility for a California medical license. However, exceptional candidates with a PhD degree are also encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will receive competitive compensation and appointment at the appropriate academic level (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) commensurate with experience and ac­complishments. Apply here. Applicants should upload curriculum vitae and names of three references.  For further inquiries please contact:  Preet Chaudhary, MD, PhD, Chief of Nohl Division of Hematology, Keck School of Medicine of USC, 1441 Eastlake Avenue, NOR 3468, MC 9172, Los Angeles, CA 90033. For further inquiries, Email: Preet.chaudhary@med.usc.edu Job ID REQ20172412 Posted Date 03/06/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the lates