    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-associate-professor-of-neurology-practitioner-chla/1209/92187558672": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate Professor of Neurology (Practitioner) CHLA",
      "description": "Clinical Associate Professor of Neurology (Practitioner) CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Associate Professor of Neurology (Practitioner) CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20171921 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) TThe University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Division of Neurology, Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) and the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California (USC) are actively seeking a neurologist with training in child neurology and neuromuscular medicine as a full-time faculty member for the position of Clinical Associate of Neurology and Pediatrics (Practitioner) and as a division director for CHLA’s neuromuscular program. Neuromuscular Program : CHLA’s neuromuscular program is one of the largest and most diverse in the United States, offering state of the art interventions in gene therapy. The division director will oversee over a dozen clinical trials, multidisciplinary care clinics, a CCS02-accredited clinical program, and will work with the Chief of Neurology and Chair of Pediatrics to guide advances in neuromuscular clinical care, engagement in cutting-edge clinical trials, and research. In this latter capacity, an option to take on a role as the director of research for the neurological institute is available to qualified and interested individuals. Finally, the division director will be responsible for leading educational initiatives for pediatric, child neurology, and adult neurology trainees with other members of the neuromuscular team. Division of Neurology CHLA is a busy urban, academic, teaching hospital with a diverse patient population. Our program has access to specialists in multiple areas of neurology including epilepsy, movement disorders, neurocritical care, neuroimmunology and neurodevelopmental disorders. Our faculty provide inpatient and outpatient clinical services to CHLA and five satellite clinic locations within the greater Los Angeles area. The division has an ACGME-approved child neurology residency program which operates in collaboration with the Keck School of Medicine, Los Angeles General Hospital, and the Keck USC/University Hospital. In addition our division has multiple fellowships in epilepsy, epilepsy genetics, neuroimmunology, neurocritical care, and movement disorders. The division of neurology and the neurological institute are dedicated to advancing programs in basic, translational and clinical research, boasting an annual NIH budget of over 25 million dollars. The annual base salary range for this position is $116,505-$417,709. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. For inquiries, please contact: Jonathan D. Santoro, MD Las Madrinas Endowed Chair and Chief of Neurology Associate Professor of Neurology and Pediatrics Children’s Hospital Los Angeles | Keck School of Medicine of USC Email: jdsantoro@chla.usc.edu | Phone: 323-361-4643 . Job ID REQ20171921 Posted Date 02/27/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching 