    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-instructors-of-radiology-fellow/1209/89232361600": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructors of Radiology (Fellow)",
      "description": "Clinical Instructors of Radiology (Fellow) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructors of Radiology (Fellow) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20169659 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department is comprised of over 40 academically and clinically active faculty, 5 research faculty and a highly competitive training program of 17 fellows and 43 residents from across the country. The Department of Radiology at the University of Southern California Keck School of Medicine (KSoM) is recruiting candidates for fellowship positions, in both our Non-ACGME and ACGME accredited programs to join the Department in the following sections. Non-ACGME fellowship programs: Body Imaging and Intervention, Body/Breast, Body/CTI, Breast Imaging , Musculoskeletal, PET, and 3D Advanced Visualization.  Those interested in Non-ACGME fellowships, please apply directly with program directors (see below). ACGME programs: Nuclear Medicine/PET, Neuroradiology, Vascular/Interventional. Those interested in ACGME fellowships, please apply through the match. We are located on the Health Science campus near Downtown Los Angeles. Our hospitals include Keck Hospital of USC, USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center and Hospital, LA General Medical Center, and USC Verdugo Hills Hospital. Outpatient sites include a full-service outpatient imaging center and PET/CT center. Each site has a different character, serving distinct patient populations but treating a wide variety of disease processes. We have some of the most advanced imaging facilities for state-of-the-art imaging and operate an active molecular imaging facility and cyclotron for novel compound production.  We also have a 4D lab group available for image construction and quantitative analysis and collaboration. University benefits include a housing stipend of $10,000 and $2,000 in academic funds. Base salary : $92,000 The USC Department of Radiology is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic community. We believe that diversity is integral to excellence and welcome applications from all individuals whose backgrounds or interests align with this commitment. Interested Non-ACGME candidates may submit a curriculum vitae and cover letter to the following Program Directors: Non-ACGME fellowship programs : Policies (scardweb.org) Body Imaging and Intervention:   Ali Rastegarpour, MD ali.rastegarpour@med.usc.edu Body/CTI:                                  Lucia Flors-Blasco, MD lucia.flors-blasco@med.usc.edu Breast/Body                         Sandy Lee, MD slee6@dhs.lacount.gov & Ali Rastegarpour, MD ali.rastegarpour@med.usc.edu Breast Imaging:                          Sandy Lee, MD slee6@dhs.lacount.gov Musculoskeletal:                         Dani Sarohia, MD dani.sarohia@med.usc.edu PET: Peter Conti, MD peter.conti@med.usc.edu 3D Advanced Visualization: Summer Decker, PhD summer.decker@med.usc.edu ACGME accredited Programs - FREIDA™ AMA Residency & Fellowship Programs Database (ama-assn.org ). Nuclear Medicine:                       Patrick Colletti, MD Colletti@med.usc.edu Neuroradiology                          Alexander Lerner, MD alerner@dhs.lacounty.gov Vascular/Interventional                Sue Hanks, MD shanks@dhs.lacounty.gov Job ID REQ20169659 Posted Date 12/06/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news,