    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-instructor-of-emergency-medicine-fellow/1209/88690688016": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Emergency Medicine (Fellow)",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor of Emergency Medicine (Fellow) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructor of Emergency Medicine (Fellow) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20169557 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Keck School of Medicine at the University of Southern California (USC) is seeking qualified emergency medicine physicians to join its Department of Emergency Medicine fellowship programs, which include Ultrasound, Research, Education, EMS, and Health Science Systems. This position is designed for physicians who are board-certified or board-eligible in Emergency Medicine (ABEM or ABOEM) and who demonstrate excellence in clinical care, teaching, and scholarly engagement. Fellows will receive advanced training while contributing to the supervision and education of residents and medical students. Position Details: Academic appointment as Clinical Instructor at the Keck School of Medicine. Competitive annual salary range: $90,000–$100,000 , based on experience and qualifications. Includes excellent university benefits and access to USC’s professional development resources. Eligibility Requirements: Must hold an active and unrestricted California medical license by the start of the fellowship. Must be board-certified or board-eligible in Emergency Medicine. Must meet all Medical Board of California licensing requirements, including: Completion of an accredited residency program. Additional Considerations: USC considers multiple factors when extending offers, including scope of responsibilities, candidate qualifications, internal equity, and compliance with federal, state, and local laws. All fellows must complete institutional credentialing and privileging prior to clinical duties. Job ID REQ20169557 Posted Date 11/21/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn Mor