    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/anatomic-pathology-assistant-associate-or-professor-of-clinical-pathology/1209/88557856176": {
      "title": "Anatomic Pathology - Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology",
      "description": "Anatomic Pathology - Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Anatomic Pathology - Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Pathology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20169146 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) Anatomic Pathology – Genitourinary Pathology University of Southern California, Keck School of Medicine Open Rank, Clinical or Clinician Educator Series The Department of Pathology and Laboratory Medicine of the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California is seeking to fill a full-time faculty position (open rank) with an outstanding, academically-oriented candidate with sub-specialty fellowship training in Genitourinary Pathology. The successful candidate will serve the needs of a busy practice at Keck Hospital of USC and USC/Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center and Hospital.  The appointee will contribute to the education of medical students, residents and surgical pathology fellows. Applicants must hold an MD or DO degree, be eligible for an unrestricted California Medical License and be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Anatomic Pathology.  The Department values experience in translational and/or clinical research.  The appointment will be in the Clinical or Clinician Educator series.  Academic rank and salary are commensurate with qualifications. Interested candidates should apply online utilizing one of the following links and submit a letter of interest, their curriculum vitae and a minimum of four academic references: Apply here and upload CV and 3 references. USC is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. USC observes affirmative action obligations consistent with state and federal law. We provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities. Applicants with questions about access or requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact USC Human Resources by phone at (213) 821-8100, or by email at uschr@usc.edu . Inquiries will be treated as confidential to the extent permitted by law.” The annual base salary range for this position is $220,000-$400.000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20169146 Posted Date 11/18/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore