    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-associate-professor-of-anesthesiology-clinician-educator-chla/1209/88557856128": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate Professor of Anesthesiology (Clinician Educator) CHLA",
      "description": "Clinical Associate Professor of Anesthesiology (Clinician Educator) CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Associate Professor of Anesthesiology (Clinician Educator) CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20169145 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Keck School of Medicine (KSOM) of the University of Southern California (USC) and Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) in the Department of Anesthesiology Critical Care Medicine, are actively seeking a full-time faculty member for the position of Attending in Pediatric Anesthesiology at the rank of Clinical Associate Professor of Anesthesiology (Clinician Educator). Academic rank will be commensurate with training and achievement. The Department is responsible for nearly 20,000 anesthetics per year with over 1000 cardiac cases and for the care of over 2400 ICU admissions. Children’s Hospital Los Angeles is a free-standing, academic children’s center with the full scope of pediatric practice and excellent educational opportunities located on Sunset Blvd in Hollywood.  We are ranked within the top 10 nationally in the most recent US News & World Report survey. The Hospital has its own research foundation and is within the top five children’s hospitals receiving federal funding. This is an outstanding opportunity for a fellowship-trained Pediatric Anesthesiologist seeking to build an academic career in a high acuity pediatric hospital. We are particularly interested in candidates with an interest in Abdominal Organ Transplantation and/or Pediatric Pain Medicine. Applicants must have successfully completed an ACGME-accredited fellowship in Pediatric Anesthesiology and be board-certified (or eligible to become board-certified within one year of hire) in Pediatric Anesthesiology. Children's Hospital Los Angeles is a premier teaching hospital and has been affiliated with the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California since 1932. The annual base salary range for this position is $480,000-$501,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. This is an outstanding opportunity in beautiful Southern California.  For further information please contact: Rosie Zesati, MAM, C-TAGME Department of Anesthesiology Critical Care Medicine Children’s Hospital Los Angeles 4650 Sunset Blvd., MS #3 Los Angeles, CA 90027 Phone:  323-361-5591 Fax: 323-361-1001 rzesati@chla.usc.edu Job ID REQ20169145 Posted Date 11/18/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page 