    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-medicine-clinician-educator-hospitalist/1209/87749983488": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator) Hospitalist",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator) Hospitalist at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Medicine (Clinician Educator) Hospitalist Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20168423 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. We strongly value diversity and are committed to equal opportunity in employment. The Division of Hospital and Palliative (HPM) at the Keck School of Medicine of USC seeks exceptional Internal Medicine Hospitalists to join our division. These are unique full-time faculty positions with an emphasis on inpatient clinical practice at Keck Medical Center of USC. Clinical responsibilities within the Division include rotations at Keck Medical Center of USC with teaching responsibilities as well as direct patient care with co-management of select surgical patients. The Hospital Medicine Program provides 24/7 coverage with hospitalists covering a handful of nights per year and approximately 12-16 weekends. Full time Nocturnist positions are also available for those applicants seeking this type of position. In addition to their inpatient clinical responsibilities, selected applicants will have significant opportunities to engage in the development of students and residents. As faculty within the Keck School of Medicine, our clinical team engages with students at varying levels of medical school while on our clinical services. The clinical program also offers a unique opportunity to provide oversight over learners from three different residency programs on our clinical teams. This diverse and broad exposure to learners allows for formal teaching opportunities at the medical school level, engagement in varying resident didactic sessions, and participation in education conferences. Selected applicants will be expected to engage in such extracurricular professional and development activities as well as participate in medical center committee membership and quality and safety improvement initiatives. Applicants should demonstrate a dedication to caring for a diverse patient population, a passion for teaching learners at various levels, excellent communication skills, and an enthusiasm for working in a collegial team-based environment. The annual base salary range for this position is $270,000-$290,000 .  When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC provides a broad range of benefits to help protect your (and your family’s) health, wealth, and future – like health insurance, wellness programs, generous retirement plan options, life insurance, and tuition benefits. This position typically has a start date aligned with the start of the Academic Year (July 1). Applicants must be board-certified or board-eligible in Internal Medicine and hold a current CA State Medical License and a full schedule, fee paid DEA License with a CA address at the time of credentialing. Job ID REQ20168423 Posted Date 10/27/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Dis