    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-instructor-of-neurology-fellow/1209/79535625248": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Neurology (Fellow)",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor of Neurology (Fellow) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructor of Neurology (Fellow) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20160814 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Neurology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California is offering a one and/or two-year Non-ACGME Clinical Fellowship with emphasis on Multiple Sclerosis, Headache, General Neurology, Movement Disorders and Intraoperative Neurophysiologic Monitoring (IOM). Candidates must have completed an accredited neurology residency program and be eligible for medical licensure in the state of California. Neurology junior faculty members are dedicated to training residents and medical students.  The position offers a competitive salary with excellent university benefits and an academic appointment of Neurology Fellow at the USC Keck School of Medicine. The annual base salary for this position is $90,019. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Apply here and please submit your curriculum vitae to: Helena Chui, M.D., Chair, Department of Neurology, 1540 Alcazar Street, CHP 215, Los Angeles, CA  90033.  Phone (323)442-7686, email: chui@usc.edu Job ID REQ20160814 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC D