      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Medicine (Fellow) Division of Transplant Nephrology",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor of Medicine (Fellow) Division of Transplant Nephrology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Instructor of Medicine (Fellow) Division of Transplant Nephrology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20157832 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. University of Southern California, Department of Medicine, Division of Nephrology and Hypertension, offers a fellowship in Transplant Nephrology. The fellowship is a one-year AST-accredited program designed to provide Nephrology graduates with experience in all aspects of kidney transplantation. The curriculum will provide trainees with the foundation needed to become successful among the next generation of Transplant Nephrologists, program directors, clinicians, and medical educators. The fellowship includes involvement in medical education, patient safety, quality improvement, and utilization management. Clinical rotations take place at the Keck Medical Center (KMC) of USC, a private 411 bed hospital. KMC has full UNOS accreditation for multi-organ transplantation including kidney, liver, pancreas, heart and lung transplant . The annual base salary for this position is $96,118.29. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Apply here and for more information or inquiry on application prerequisites, please contact: Lodel Yerro Caplan, MHA Programs and Projects Administrator Division of Nephrology and Hypertension Keck School of Medicine of USC University of Southern California 2020 Zonal Avenue IRD 806 Los Angeles, CA 90033 E-mail: Lodel.Caplan@med.usc.edu The University of Southern California strongly values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment.  Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20157832 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & 