    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-associate-or-professor-of-clinical-neurology/1209/69366069440": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Neurology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Neurology at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant/Associate or Professor of Clinical Neurology Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20152032 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. Division of Epilepsy,  Department of Neurology, Keck School of Medicine, University of Southern California, seeks full-time Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Neurology The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Neurology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California seeks a full-time Neurologist with subspecialty training in Epilepsy. As an epileptologist you would become part of the USC Comprehensive Epilepsy Program, which is a Level IV Epilepsy Center.  Our epilepsy program serves as a tertiary referral center for an extended network of hospitals in Southern and Central California, and a leader amongst epilepsy centers in the region through our USC Epilepsy Care Consortium. Responsibilities include direct in-patient and out-patient care specific to epilepsy and epilepsy surgery, as well as continuous bedside video/EEG monitoring of patients in the EMU and ICU. Neurology faculty members are dedicated to training fellows, residents, and medical students at Keck School of Medicine. There are ample opportunities for translational research in the affiliated USC Neurorestoration Center. Candidates must be Board eligible/certified in Neurology, have completed fellowship training in Epilepsy, and be eligible for medical licensure in the State of California. The position offers a competitive salary with excellent university benefits, and an academic appointment commensurate with experience and qualifications at the Assistant, or Associate Professor level at the USC Keck School of Medicine. The annual base salary range for this position is $220,000-240,000.  When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Apply here and please submit your curriculum vitae to: Patricia Leyva Patricia.Leyva@med.usc.edu , Epilepsy Clinical Program Administrator;  Helena Chui, M.D. helena.chui@med.usc.edu, Chair Department of Neurology; or Ryan McGinn MD, ryan.mcginn@med.usc.edu, Division of Epilepsy, USC Keck School of Medicine, 1520 San Pablo Street, Los Angeles, CA 90033. Job ID REQ20152032 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsi