    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-dermatology-clinician-educator-chla/1209/60632245680": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Dermatology (Clinician Educator) CHLA",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Dermatology (Clinician Educator) CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Dermatology (Clinician Educator) CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20141638 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Dermatology at the Keck School of Medicine of the University of Southern California is seeking outstanding applicants for a full-time position as an Assistant Professor for our Pediatric Dermatology Division. Candidates must be eligible for licensure in California and have strong clinical skills and interest in serving a diverse patient population. The successful candidate will be a fellowship trained Pediatric Dermatologist and board certified in Pediatrics and Dermatology. We offer a competitive salary package with excellent benefits. The annual base salary cap for this position is $260,000.  When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment. Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20141638 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become available. Sign Up Job Alerts Don't see what you’re looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when roles become available. All fields are required. First name Last name Email address Interested In Select a Job Category OR School/Division from the list of options. Finally, click \"Add\" to create your job alert. Job Category Select a Job Category Academic Advising Academic Advising and Career Counseling Accounting, Finance and Banking Administration Administrative Support Athletics Auxiliary Services Biomedical Business and Financial Management Child Care Services Clinical Administration Compliance Data Analysis Dentistry Development and Fundraising Environmental Health and Safety Facilities Management Facilities Management and Construction Faculty Faculty and Teaching Faculty Development Genetics Grants Administration & Sponsored Programs Health and Medical Services Human