    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/solid-tumor-program-medical-director-associate-or-professor-of-clinical-pediatrics-hematology-oncol/1209/60632244944": {
      "title": "Solid Tumor Program Medical Director Associate or Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Hematology-Oncology)-CHLA",
      "description": "Solid Tumor Program Medical Director Associate or Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Hematology-Oncology)-CHLA at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Solid Tumor Program Medical Director Associate or Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Hematology-Oncology)-CHLA Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20138564 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Cancer and Blood Disease Institute (CBDI) at the Children’s Hospital Los Angeles (CHLA) and the Division of Hematology-Oncology within the Department of Pediatrics, Keck School of Medicine, University of Southern California (USC) are recruiting an internationally recognized leader to serve as the Medical Director of the Solid Tumor Program. This individual will oversee clinical and research activities, and work with CBDI leadership on Program expansion. They will be expected to conduct research and further advance a leading research program that integrates laboratory and clinical science to develop and deliver innovative cancer therapies for pediatric solid tumors. The position reports to the CBDI Section Head for Oncology. The position includes membership at the USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center and an academic appointment through USC Keck School of Medicine at the level of Associate Professor or Professor, appropriate to training and experience. The CBDI is the largest and top-ranked pediatric hematology-oncology program in the western U.S. The U.S. News & World Report ranked the CBDI #3 and CHLA #7 in the nation in 2023-24. The Solid Tumor Program saw approximately 100 new patients in 2022. The Program is dedicated to providing the best possible multidisciplinary, individualized care for children with solid tumors including sarcomas, neuroblastoma, retinoblastoma, liver tumors, and kidney tumors. The Program conducts leading-edge research to discover, develop and deliver therapies designed to improve outcomes. The CBDI has a large clinical trials operation. Two leading, international pediatric oncology clinical trials consortia are headquartered within the CBDI: New Approaches to Neuroblastoma Therapy (NANT) and the Therapeutic Advances in Childhood Leukemia/Lymphoma (TACL). The CBDI is also an active member of 20 leading international consortia. CBDI investigators conduct extensive bench-to-bedside research. Research funding in FY23 totaled $52.5 million with $8.3 million in new awards. The CBDI hosts an ACGME-accredited pediatric hematology-oncology fellowship training program and 1-year advanced subspecialty fellowships in AYA Oncology, Neuro-Oncology, Transplantation/Cellular Therapy and Coagulation. The annual base salary range for this position is $116,505-$517,500.  When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Strong administrative, clinical, research and financial support will be provided, including staff, infrastructure, endowments, and institutional resources. CHLA and USC are equal opportunity, affirmative action employers. The division greatly values diversity and is committed to building a vibrant and culturally diverse community of faculty that best reflects the patients and families we serve. Individuals from underrepresented groups in medicine are especially encouraged to apply. For inquiries, please contact: Alan S. Wayne, M.D. Director, Cancer and Blood Disease Institute Chief, Division of Hematology-Oncology Vice Chair, Department of Pediatrics Children's Hospital Los Angeles Associate Director, USC Norris Comprehensive Cancer Center Professor of Pediatrics and Medicine Keck School of Medicine University of Southern California Alfred E. Mann Family Foundation Chair in Cancer Research awayne@chla.usc.edu Job ID REQ20138564 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law Positions (Open Rank) Los Angeles, California No Saved Jobs. View All Jobs No Recently Viewed Jobs. View All Jobs Sign Up for Job Alerts Don't see what you're looking for? Sign up and we'll notify you when new roles become av