    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor-of-radiology-part-time/1209/91449067312": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiology (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiology (Part-Time) at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor of Radiology (Part-Time) Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20124777 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Department of Radiology at the Keck School of Medicine of USC is recruiting a part- or full-time, fellowship trained radiologist to join the department. The candidate will be appointed to a faculty rank commensurate with their experience/qualifications. Applicants must be ABR board-certified, -eligible or equivalent The candidate will participate in the abdominal imaging section as well as our community radiology specialist section.  This position is for both the Keck Medicine of USC Health Science Campus and the USC Verdugo Hills Hospital. Our Community Radiology Specialist section is the predominant provider of imaging services at Verdugo Hills Hospital bringing a multidisciplinary approach delivering excellence in diagnostic CT, MR, US, fluoroscopic imaging as well as advanced image guided procedures. By bringing together the expertise of physicians from the community and Keck Medicine, we provide exceptional, comprehensive care across a broad spectrum of specialties. The Department is comprised of 65 faculty, 15 fellows and 47 residents.  We have both accredited residency and fellowship programs.  Our hospitals include Keck Hospital of USC, USC Norris Cancer Hospital, VHH, Los Angeles County Medical Center (LAC+USC).  Outpatient sites include a full-service outpatient imaging center and PET/CT center. The USC DOR is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive academic community. We believe that diversity is integral to excellence and welcome applications from all individuals whose backgrounds or interests align with this commitment. Interested individuals may apply here and upload a curriculum vitae and cover letter (addressed to Robert K. Ryu MD, Chair and Professor, USC Department of Radiology. The University of Southern California strongly values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment.  Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20124777 Posted Date 02/06/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career at USC can help you grow, contribute, and make an impact through opportunities, professional development, and a community committed to excellence and innovation. Learn More June 02, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Employee Transit Subsidy The USC Transit Subsidy Program helps employees save on public transportation while reducing single-passenger commuting. Learn More July 28, 2026 Benefits & Perks Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Load more Jobs for You Featured Jobs Saved Jobs Viewed Jobs Save Job Senior Financial Analyst - Revenue Cycle Operations - Full Time 8 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job EVS Worker - Environmental Services - Per Diem 8 Hour Rotating (Non-Exempt) (Union) Los Angeles, California Save Job Physician Assistant II - Vascular Surgery - Full Time 10 Hour Days (Exempt) (Non-Union) Glendale, California Save Job Professor of Law, Associate Professor of Law, and Assistant Professor of Law P