    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/hospitalist-clinician-educator-division-of-inpatient-pediatrics-lac-usc/1209/60632242336": {
      "title": "Hospitalist, Clinician Educator-Division of Inpatient Pediatrics LAC USC",
      "description": "Hospitalist, Clinician Educator-Division of Inpatient Pediatrics LAC USC at USC We use cookies and other tracking technologies to support navigation, to improve our products and services, to support our marketing activities and to provide content from third parties.To manage your preferences, select \"Manage Settings\" or choose \"Accept\" to consent to the use of Cookies. Accept Manage Settings Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Matching job links will appear below as you type. Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to select. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Hospitalist, Clinician Educator-Division of Inpatient Pediatrics LAC+USC Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20116918 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The University of Southern California Keck School of Medicine Department of Pediatrics at LAC+USC Medical Center is seeking a qualified candidate for a full-time faculty position as an Assistant Professor of Clinical Pediatrics (Clinician educator tract) with the Division of Inpatient and Critical Care Pediatrics. The position will involve integration into an existing service that provides in-house 24/7 care. Candidates must be board certified in pediatrics and have a valid California medical license. Candidates with post graduate experience with inpatient care, a strong interest in teaching and working with students and residents, and a passion for working with the underserved, are preferred. “The annual base salary range for this position is $150,000- $180,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations.” Apply here and upload  CV and letter of interest to: Jeffrey L. Johnson M.D. (jeffreyl@usc.edu) Director of Pediatric Inpatient and Critical Care Services Department of Pediatrics / LAC+USC Medical Center 2020 Zonal Avenue, IRD Rm 101 Los Angeles, CA 90033 The University of Southern California strongly values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment.  Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20116918 Posted Date 07/25/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of huma