    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/assistant-professor-of-clinical-surgery-hepatobiliary-pancreatic-surgery-abdominal-organ-transplant/1209/88705822528": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Surgery Hepatobiliary/Pancreatic Surgery/Abdominal Organ Transplantation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Surgery Hepatobiliary/Pancreatic Surgery/Abdominal Organ Transplantation at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Assistant Professor of Clinical Surgery Hepatobiliary/Pancreatic Surgery/Abdominal Organ Transplantation Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20102782 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The University of Southern California (USC), founded in 1880, is the largest private employer in the City of Los Angeles. As an employee of USC, you will be a part of a world-class research university and a member of the \"Trojan Family,\" which is comprised of the faculty, students and staff that make the university what it is. The Division of Hepatobiliary/Pancreatic Surgery and Abdominal Organ Transplantation within the Department of Surgery at the Keck School of Medicine of the Univeristy of Southern California is recruiting for a HPB surgeon at the Assistant Professor of Clinical Surgery level. The candidate must be BC/BE by American Board of Surgery and be ASTS & HPB Surgery certified and proficient in all aspects of HPB surgery. Qualified candidates will be involved in the care of patients, teaching residents, collaboration in research, continuing education, and developing outreach activities of the Division in surrounding counties. The University of Southern California strongly values diversity and is committed to equal opportunity in employment.  Women and men, and members of all racial and ethnic groups, people with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. Job ID REQ20102782 Posted Date 11/22/2025 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good. Learn More February 24, 2026 USC News Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content Career Development at USC Discover how a career 