    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/clinical-assistant-professor/1209/96947697408": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Clinical Assistant Professor Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174916 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Herman Ostrow School of Dentistry of USC seeks applicants for a part-time (50% FTE), non-tenure track position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor of Dentistry in the Department of Dental Public Health and Community Outreach for the Section of Mobile Clinic Programs. Responsibilities include clinical supervision and instruction of USC dental students at affiliated satellite mobile community clinics within Los Angeles, serving mainly children and adolescents, and coordination of services and auxiliary staff at these sites, as well as some teaching at the pre-doctoral level at the School and School clinics. Candidates must have a DDS or DMD degree and be licensed to practice in the State of California. Candidates with additional education (MS, MPH), clinical training (AEGD, GPR, Advanced Pediatric Training), and/or strong experience caring for underserved children are highly encouraged to apply. Interested applicants must submit a cover letter, a complete curriculum vitae, and arrange to provide at least three letters of reference. Consideration of applicants will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. The hourly rate for this position is $56.65 - $63.00. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state, and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. USC is an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, protected veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law or USC policy. Job ID REQ20174916 Posted Date 06/26/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories 