    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/visiting-faculty-position-in-economics/1209/94510044576": {
      "title": "Visiting Faculty Position in Economics",
      "description": "Visiting Faculty Position in Economics at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Visiting Faculty Position in Economics Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174537 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Economics in the Dana and David Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences at the University of Southern California invites outstanding candidates to fill a full-time teaching-track visiting faculty position -- Visiting Assistant Professor, Visiting Associate Professor, and Visiting Professor -- with an anticipated start date of Fall 2026. We are looking for candidates with strong interests in teaching econometrics and/or courses that teach or use data science methods, at the undergraduate and master’s levels . Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Economics and previous teaching experience in the subject area.  Please submit a cover letter, CV, and teaching evaluation record. Please also provide the names of three individuals who will be contacted by USC for letters of reference. Referees should speak to teaching abilities. In order to be considered for this position, all candidates must apply via the \"Apply\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The annual base salary range for this position is $80,000 - $125,000. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20174537 Posted Date 04/29/2026 Apply Save Job Current employees apply here SHARE Facebook X LinkedIn Email Related Content Learn More August 04, 2025 USC Today Explore the latest stories of impact, innovation, and Trojan spirit shaping USC and the world beyond. Learn More July 28, 2025 USC News Blog - Hub Page Related Content Our Communities Rooted in LA, USC partners with local communities to uplift education, well-being, and opportunity across Southern California. Learn More July 28, 2025 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content Mission Statement USC’s central mission is the development of human beings and society as a whole through the cultivation and enrichment of the human mind and spirit. Learn More July 28, 2025 Mission & Values Blog - Hub Page Related Content Alumni USC Today’s Alumni page highlights news, achievements, research and stories from USC alumni and the Trojan Family. Learn More August 03, 2026 Culture & Community Article Blog - Hub Page Related Content USC Football Stay connected with USC Football through the latest news, schedules, scores, highlights, and team updates. Learn More September 10, 2026 Culture & Community Blog - Hub Page Related Content AI at USC At USC, artificial intelligence is more than just code. It is a catalyst for discovery, creativity and social good.