    "https://usccareers.usc.edu/job/los-angeles/part-time-teaching-track-faculty-position-in-physical-education-and-mind-body-health/1209/94510044512": {
      "title": "Part-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Physical Education & Mind Body Health",
      "description": "Part-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Physical Education & Mind Body Health at USC Skip to main content Life at USC Career Areas Faculty Keck Medicine of USC Auxiliary Services Information Technology Services Human Resources, Ethics, and Compliance USC Advancement Current Employees Returning Applicants Saved Jobs 0 Job Alerts Join Our Trojan Community At USC, we are united by shared values and a bold vision for the future. Join a workplace where your role has meaning, your growth is supported, and your impact is felt across campus, Los Angeles, and the world. Search by Keyword Search Jobs Faculty Educators, mentors, and agents of change. As USC faculty, we are committed to advancing knowledge, inspiring students, and elevating research that fosters discovery and drives societal impact – all in service of our mission. Learn more on the We Are USC Faculty webpage Search Jobs Search by Keyword Location Radius Select Radius 5 miles 15 miles 25 miles 35 miles 50 miles Search Jobs Part-Time, Teaching-Track Faculty Position in Physical Education & Mind Body Health Los Angeles, CA Apply Save Job Current employees apply here Job ID REQ20174462 Category Faculty Helpful Information for Applicants External Applicants Internal Applicants (Current USC Employees) The Department of Physical Education & Mind Body Health in the Dana and David Dornsife College of Letters, Arts and Sciences at the University of Southern California in Los Angeles, California provides a variety of opportunities for students to improve their general health and fitness through fitness and wellness activities and classroom lecture classes. We are seeking outstanding candidates for a part-time instructor position for the 2026-2027 academic year. Qualified applicants should have a strong background in Physical Education, Kinesiology, Recreation, or related fields, possess certifications in related fitness areas, and have demonstrated excellence in teaching a variety of fitness courses. Under the guidance of the Director of Physical Education & Mind Body Health, the primary responsibilities will include instruction of activity-based fitness and classroom lecture courses. Our pedagogy philosophy is to make an impact on students’ overall wellbeing through teaching and building community, through a diverse, equitable, and inclusive learning environment. Minimum Qualifications Master’s Degree in any of the following: · Kinesiology · Physical Education · Exercise Science · Recreational Sport/Administration · Education (with an emphasis in Physical Education, Kinesiology, Physiology of Exercise or Adaptive Physical Education) Bachelor's Degree in any of the following: · Any Life Science · Dance · Physiology · Health Education · Recreational Sports · Physical Therapy or the equivalent Additional Preferred Qualifications A Master’s degree is preferred. Promotion opportunities are available for those with a Master’s degree. Faculty with a Bachelor’s degree will be provided with a one-year appointment. Prior teaching experience in college-level courses and/or training certifications in the domains of wellness, health, and fitness. To be considered for this position, applicants are required to submit an electronic application, professional vitae, letter of interest and the names of at least three references who can speak to your teaching experience. In order to be considered for this position, all candidates must apply via the \"Apply\" link at the top or bottom of this page. The per course rate for this position is $2,750. When extending an offer of employment, the University of Southern California considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, the candidate’s work experience, education/training, key skills, internal peer equity, federal, state and local laws, contractual stipulations, grant funding, as well as external market and organizational considerations. Job ID REQ20174462 Posted Date 04/29/2026 A